// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 搭配詞 轉承詞 Connectives (tools/colloc_emit.py)
window.JC_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"however – while","cards":[{"w":"It was raining hard. However, we still went out to play.","p":"conj.","d":"however · 對比","c":"雨下得很大。然而，我們還是出去玩了。","s":"The weather was very cold this morning. However, my brother still rode his bike to school as usual."},{"w":"The test was hard. However, most of the students passed it.","p":"conj.","d":"however · 對比","c":"考試很難。然而，大部分學生都通過了。","s":"The math homework was really difficult last night. However, Mary finished all of it before ten o'clock."},{"w":"I like the dress. However, it is too expensive for me.","p":"conj.","d":"however · 對比","c":"我喜歡這件洋裝。然而，它對我來說太貴了。","s":"Those new shoes in the store window look great. However, they cost too much money for a student like me."},{"w":"however, + 逗號；放句首或句中，不能像 but 直接連接兩句","p":"conj.","d":"however · 對比","c":"however 後要加逗號；不能像 but 一樣直接連接兩個句子","s":"Tom wanted to join the soccer game. However, his mother asked him to clean his room first."},{"w":"I wanted to go to the party, but I had to study.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 對比","c":"我想去派對，但我必須讀書。","s":"My sister loves to eat ice cream in summer, but she gets a stomachache every time she eats too much."},{"w":"The food was cheap, but it tasted really good.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 對比","c":"食物很便宜，但味道真的很好。","s":"The small restaurant near our school looks old, but the noodles there are the best in town."},{"w":"She is very short, but she plays basketball well.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 對比","c":"她很矮，但籃球打得很好。","s":"Grandpa is already eighty years old, but he still walks to the park every morning to exercise."},{"w":"but 不與 although 連用；兩句間用逗號","p":"conj.","d":"but · 對比","c":"but 不可與 although 同時使用","s":"The bus was late again today, but I still got to school before the first class began."},{"w":"Nobody but Tom knew the answer to the question.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 其他用法","c":"除了湯姆，沒人知道這題的答案。","s":"Nobody but Lisa remembered to bring an umbrella, so we all got wet on the way home from school."},{"w":"Everyone came to the party but Mary.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 其他用法","c":"除了瑪麗，大家都來派對了。","s":"All the students but Jack handed in their homework on time, so the teacher talked to him after class."},{"w":"I have nothing but love for my family.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 其他用法","c":"我對家人只有愛。","s":"After the long trip, we had nothing but bread and water in the kitchen, so Dad went to the store."},{"w":"The last but one is my house.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 其他用法","c":"倒數第二間是我家。","s":"The last but one house on this street is my aunt's, and she always makes cookies for us."},{"w":"but 當介係詞","p":"conj.","d":"but · 其他用法","c":"除了 (= except)：nobody but / all but / nothing but (只有)=but 介係詞表「除了」","s":"Everyone in my class but Peter likes the new music teacher because she lets us sing and dance."},{"w":"not…but… (不是…而是)：He is not a teacher but a doctor.","p":"conj.","d":"but · 易混淆","c":"not…but 表「不是…而是」","s":"My uncle is not a doctor but a nurse, and he works in a big hospital near the train station."},{"w":"He is only ten, yet he can cook dinner for his family.","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 對比","c":"他才十歲，卻能為家人做晚餐。","s":"My little sister is only eight, yet she can swim faster than most of the older kids in the pool."},{"w":"The room is small, yet it is clean and comfortable.","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 對比","c":"房間很小，卻乾淨又舒適。","s":"The apartment is old and small, yet it is close to the MRT station and very cheap to rent."},{"w":"I studied all night, yet I still failed the test.","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 對比","c":"我整晚讀書，卻還是考不及格。","s":"Jenny practiced the piano for many hours every day, yet she was still nervous before the school show."},{"w":"yet (連接詞)","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 對比","c":"but，語氣較強；注意與 yet (副詞「還沒」) 不同=連接詞 yet 等於 but","s":"It was raining hard outside, yet the kids ran to the playground to play soccer in the mud."},{"w":"Have you finished your homework yet?","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 其他用法","c":"你作業寫完了嗎？","s":"Have you cleaned your room yet, or are you going to wait until Mom gets home from work?"},{"w":"I haven't seen that movie yet.","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 其他用法","c":"我還沒看那部電影。","s":"I haven't tried the new noodle shop next to the park yet, but my friends say it is wonderful."},{"w":"Not yet. Give me five more minutes.","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 其他用法","c":"還沒。再給我五分鐘。","s":"Mom asked if dinner was ready, and Dad said not yet because the chicken needed ten more minutes."},{"w":"This is her best song yet.","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 其他用法","c":"這是她到目前為止最好的歌。","s":"Our team played very well tonight, and the coach said it was our best game yet this year."},{"w":"yet 當副詞","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 其他用法","c":"還沒／已經（問句、否定句句尾）；best…yet = 到目前為止=yet 副詞多用於問句與否定句句尾","s":"Has the mailman come yet, or should I wait a little longer for the letter from my cousin in Japan?"},{"w":"I haven't eaten yet. / I have already eaten. / I am still eating.","p":"conj.","d":"yet · 易混淆","c":"我還沒吃。／我已經吃了。／我還在吃。","s":"I haven't read the new comic book yet, although my brother has already read it two times this week."},{"w":"I like tea, while my sister likes coffee.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 對比","c":"我喜歡茶，而我妹妹喜歡咖啡。","s":"My father enjoys watching baseball games on TV, while my mother would rather read a book in the garden."},{"w":"Some students work hard, while others just play all day.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 對比","c":"有些學生很努力，而有些則整天玩。","s":"Some people in my class love hot summer days, while others cannot wait for the cool weather of fall."},{"w":"Tom is tall and thin, while his brother is short and fat.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 對比","c":"湯姆又高又瘦，而他哥哥又矮又胖。","s":"Our old music room was dark and noisy, while the new one is bright, quiet, and has a big window."},{"w":"While I was cooking dinner, the phone rang twice.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 時間","c":"我正在做晚餐時，電話響了兩次。","s":"While Mom was talking on the phone in the kitchen, the dog ate all the cookies on the table."},{"w":"Don't talk with your friends while you are eating.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 時間","c":"吃東西時不要和朋友講話。","s":"Please don't play with your phone while the teacher is explaining the new lesson to the class."},{"w":"My dad read the paper while my mom watched TV.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 時間","c":"我爸爸看報紙，而我媽媽看電視。","s":"My brother watched a movie in the living room while I did my English homework upstairs in my bedroom."},{"w":"while + 進行式（當…的時候）；也可表對比「而」","p":"conj.","d":"while · 時間","c":"while 常接進行式","s":"While Tom was riding his bike to school this morning, he saw a little cat sleeping under a tree."},{"w":"While I like the idea, I don't think it will work.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 讓步","c":"雖然我喜歡這個想法，但我不認為它行得通。","s":"While the new restaurant has very good food, it is too far from our house to go there often."},{"w":"While the book is long, it is easy to read.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 讓步","c":"雖然這本書很長，但很容易讀。","s":"While my brother is good at sports, he often has trouble with his math and science homework at school."},{"w":"while (雖然) 放句首","p":"conj.","d":"while · 讓步","c":"although，語氣較輕=while 放句首可表讓步「雖然」","s":"While I understand you are tired after school, you still need to help wash the dishes tonight."},{"w":"Let's rest for a while before we go on.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 其他用法","c":"我們繼續之前先休息一會兒。","s":"After we finished cleaning the music room, the teacher let us rest for a while before the next lesson."},{"w":"I haven't seen him for a long while.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 其他用法","c":"我好一陣子沒看到他了。","s":"It has been a long while since we visited Grandma, so let's go to see her this Sunday."},{"w":"We go to the movies once in a while.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 其他用法","c":"我們偶爾去看電影。","s":"My family doesn't eat out much, but once in a while we go to a nice restaurant for dinner."},{"w":"It took quite a while to find the key.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 其他用法","c":"找鑰匙花了不少時間。","s":"It took us quite a while to find a parking space, so we were late for the movie."},{"w":"while 當名詞","p":"conj.","d":"while · 其他用法","c":"一會兒：for a while / a long while / once in a while / after a while=while 可當名詞「一段時間」","s":"After a while, the rain stopped and the children ran outside to play in the wet grass again."},{"w":"While I was sleeping, it rained.","p":"conj.","d":"while · 易混淆","c":"During the night, it rained.=我睡覺時下雨了。＝夜裡下雨了。","s":"While my parents were buying food at the supermarket, I stayed in the car and played games on my phone."}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"on the other hand – though","cards":[{"w":"The job pays well. On the other hand, the hours are long.","p":"conj.","d":"on the other hand · 對比","c":"這工作薪水不錯。另一方面，工時很長。","s":"The new mall near the station has many great stores. On the other hand, it is always crowded on weekends."},{"w":"Living in the city is fun. On the other hand, it is noisy.","p":"conj.","d":"on the other hand · 對比","c":"住在城市很有趣。另一方面，很吵。","s":"Taking the MRT to school is fast and cheap. On the other hand, it is very crowded in the morning."},{"w":"On one hand, I want to go. On the other hand, I am tired.","p":"conj.","d":"on the other hand · 對比","c":"一方面我想去。另一方面，我很累。","s":"On one hand, I want to join the basketball team. On the other hand, I need more time to study."},{"w":"on (the) one hand…on the other hand","p":"conj.","d":"on the other hand · 對比","c":"一方面…另一方面=成對使用，表兩面看法","s":"On one hand, having a dog is a lot of fun. On the other hand, you must walk it every day."},{"w":"The car is fast. On the other hand, it uses a lot of gas.","p":"conj.","d":"on the other hand · 易混淆","c":"這輛車很快。另一方面，它很耗油。","s":"This small restaurant has very good food. On the other hand, the service is slow and the chairs are hard."},{"w":"On one hand, the phone is cheap. On the other hand, it breaks easily.","p":"conj.","d":"on one hand · 對比","c":"一方面，這手機很便宜。另一方面，它很容易壞。","s":"On one hand, this new bike is very light and fast. On the other hand, it costs a lot of money."},{"w":"On one hand, I love dogs. On the other hand, they need much care.","p":"conj.","d":"on one hand · 對比","c":"一方面我愛狗。另一方面，狗需要很多照顧。","s":"On one hand, studying abroad sounds exciting. On the other hand, I would miss my friends and family very much."},{"w":"I didn't go to the movie. Instead, I stayed home and read.","p":"conj.","d":"instead · 對比","c":"我沒去看電影。我反而待在家看書。","s":"We didn't eat at the noodle shop tonight. Instead, Mom cooked fried rice and soup for the whole family."},{"w":"He didn't say sorry. Instead, he just walked away.","p":"conj.","d":"instead · 對比","c":"他沒有道歉。他反而直接走開了。","s":"Peter didn't take the bus to the station this morning. Instead, he borrowed his sister's bike and rode there."},{"w":"We had no rice, so we ate bread instead.","p":"conj.","d":"instead · 對比","c":"我們沒有米，所以改吃麵包。","s":"The movie we wanted to see was sold out, so we bought tickets for a funny cartoon instead."},{"w":"I didn't go out. Instead, I read a book. / I read a book instead of going out.","p":"conj.","d":"instead · 易混淆","c":"我沒出門。反而讀了一本書。／我讀書而沒出門。","s":"I didn't watch TV last night. Instead, I helped my little brother with his English homework for an hour."},{"w":"Instead of taking the bus, we walked to school today.","p":"conj.","d":"instead of · 對比","c":"我們今天沒搭公車，而是走路上學。","s":"Instead of eating snacks after school, Lisa now has an apple and a glass of milk every day."},{"w":"Why don't you drink water instead of soda?","p":"conj.","d":"instead of · 對比","c":"你為什麼不喝水而不要喝汽水呢？","s":"Why don't you walk to the library with me instead of sitting in front of the computer all afternoon?"},{"w":"She stayed home instead of going to the party.","p":"conj.","d":"instead of · 對比","c":"她待在家裡，而沒去派對。","s":"My dad took the train to Taichung instead of driving because the traffic on the highway was really bad."},{"w":"Unlike his brother, Tom is quiet and shy.","p":"conj.","d":"unlike · 對比","c":"和他哥哥不同，湯姆安靜又害羞。","s":"Unlike most of my friends, I really enjoy getting up early and jogging in the park before school."},{"w":"Unlike last year, it didn't snow at all this winter.","p":"conj.","d":"unlike · 對比","c":"和去年不同，今年冬天完全沒下雪。","s":"Unlike the hot and wet summer in Taiwan, the summer in that mountain town is cool and dry."},{"w":"Unlike his brother, Tom is shy. / Tom is like his father. / I don't like cold weather.","p":"conj.","d":"unlike · 易混淆","c":"和他哥哥不同，湯姆很害羞。／湯姆像他爸爸。／我不喜歡冷天氣。","s":"Unlike his father, who loves cooking, Jack doesn't like spending any time in the kitchen at all."},{"w":"Although it was cold, we went swimming in the sea.","p":"conj.","d":"although · 讓步","c":"雖然很冷，我們還是去海裡游泳。","s":"Although the restaurant was very crowded and noisy, we still had a wonderful dinner there for Grandma's birthday."},{"w":"Although he is rich, he is not happy at all.","p":"conj.","d":"although · 讓步","c":"雖然他很有錢，他一點也不快樂。","s":"Although my little brother is only six years old, he can already read many English picture books by himself."},{"w":"She passed the test, although she didn't study much.","p":"conj.","d":"although · 讓步","c":"她通過考試了，雖然她沒讀多少書。","s":"Mary went to school this morning, although she had a bad headache and didn't sleep well last night."},{"w":"although 不與 but 連用（Although…, S + V.）","p":"conj.","d":"although · 讓步","c":"although 不可與 but 同時使用","s":"Although it was raining hard, the students still played the basketball game and had a lot of fun."},{"w":"Though the bag is old, I still like it very much.","p":"conj.","d":"though · 讓步","c":"雖然這包包很舊，我還是很喜歡它。","s":"Though the old bike has only one color and no bell, Tom rides it to school happily every day."},{"w":"He went to work, though he was very sick.","p":"conj.","d":"though · 讓步","c":"他去上班了，雖然他病得很重。","s":"My grandmother still cooks dinner for the whole family every night, though she is already eighty-five years old."},{"w":"The movie was long. I enjoyed it, though.","p":"conj.","d":"though · 讓步","c":"電影很長。不過，我看得很開心。","s":"The test was really hard and took two hours. Most of the students in my class passed it, though."},{"w":"though 可放句尾當副詞（","p":"conj.","d":"though · 讓步","c":"however），前加逗號=though 放句尾等於 however","s":"The weather at the beach was cold and windy on Sunday. We still swam in the sea for an hour, though."},{"w":"The weather was cold. We had fun, though.","p":"conj.","d":"though · 其他用法","c":"天氣很冷。不過我們玩得很開心。","s":"The food at the new restaurant was not very good. The waiters were friendly and the music was nice, though."},{"w":"I don't really like the color. It's a nice dress, though.","p":"conj.","d":"though · 其他用法","c":"我不太喜歡這個顏色。不過這件洋裝很漂亮。","s":"I didn't like the ending of the movie at all. The songs in it were really beautiful, though."},{"w":"though 放句尾","p":"conj.","d":"though · 其他用法","c":"however (不過)；as though = as if (好像)=though 句尾用法與 as though","s":"My brother looked as though he had seen a ghost when he came home. He was only tired, though."}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"even though – after all","cards":[{"w":"Even though she was tired, she finished her homework.","p":"conj.","d":"even though · 讓步","c":"儘管她很累，她還是完成了作業。","s":"Even though the soup was too hot and had too much salt, the hungry boy finished the whole bowl quickly."},{"w":"He kept running even though his legs hurt a lot.","p":"conj.","d":"even though · 讓步","c":"儘管雙腿很痛，他還是繼續跑。","s":"Lisa kept practicing the song on the piano every night, even though her fingers hurt and she felt tired."},{"w":"Even though it rained, the game went on.","p":"conj.","d":"even though · 讓步","c":"儘管下雨，比賽還是繼續進行。","s":"Even though the tickets were very expensive, thousands of people came to see the famous singer at the park."},{"w":"even though 語氣比 although 強；不可寫成 even although","p":"conj.","d":"even though · 讓步","c":"even though 比 although 語氣更強","s":"Even though my parents told me the water was cold, I jumped into the swimming pool right away."},{"w":"Even if it rains tomorrow, we will go hiking.","p":"conj.","d":"even if · 讓步","c":"即使明天下雨，我們還是要去爬山。","s":"Even if the bus is late tomorrow morning, I will still get to school on time because I leave early."},{"w":"I won't tell him, even if he asks me again.","p":"conj.","d":"even if · 讓步","c":"即使他再問我，我也不會告訴他。","s":"I will finish reading this long book this weekend, even if I have to stay up late every night."},{"w":"Even if it rains, we'll go. / Even though it rained, we went. / It rained. Even so, we went.","p":"conj.","d":"even if · 易混淆","c":"即使下雨我們也會去。／儘管下雨了我們還是去了。／下雨了。即使如此，我們還是去了。","s":"Even if it is late when you get home tonight, please call me so that I know you are safe."},{"w":"It is late. Still, I want to finish this book tonight.","p":"conj.","d":"still · 讓步","c":"很晚了。儘管如此，我今晚還是想讀完這本書。","s":"I know the mountain is high and the road is long. Still, I want to climb it with my dad this summer."},{"w":"The test was hard, but he still got a high score.","p":"conj.","d":"still · 讓步","c":"考試很難，但他仍然拿了高分。","s":"The soup Mom made was not very hot, but I still liked it because it had lots of fresh vegetables."},{"w":"She is eighty, but she still goes jogging every morning.","p":"conj.","d":"still · 讓步","c":"她八十歲了，但仍然每天早上慢跑。","s":"My grandfather can't see very well now, but he still reads the newspaper every morning with his glasses on."},{"w":"Stand still while I take your picture.","p":"conj.","d":"still · 其他用法","c":"我幫你拍照時站著別動。","s":"Please stand still for a minute so that the doctor can check your eyes and ears carefully."},{"w":"The baby can't sit still for a minute.","p":"conj.","d":"still · 其他用法","c":"這寶寶一分鐘都坐不住。","s":"My little cousin cannot sit still in class, so his teacher often asks him to help hand out papers."},{"w":"Keep still, or the bee will bite you.","p":"conj.","d":"still · 其他用法","c":"別動，否則蜜蜂會咬你。","s":"Keep still and don't make any noise, or the little bird on the window will fly away quickly."},{"w":"still 當形容詞","p":"conj.","d":"still · 其他用法","c":"靜止不動的（stand still / sit still / keep still）=still 形容詞表「不動的」","s":"The lake was so still in the early morning that we could see the mountains in the water."},{"w":"It might rain. Anyway, let's go to the park.","p":"conj.","d":"anyway · 讓步","c":"可能會下雨。無論如何，我們去公園吧。","s":"I know you are tired after practice. Anyway, you have to finish your homework before you go to bed."},{"w":"I don't like him. Anyway, I will help him this time.","p":"conj.","d":"anyway · 讓步","c":"我不喜歡他。不管怎樣，這次我會幫他。","s":"The shirt is a little too big for me. Anyway, I will keep it because it was a gift from Grandma."},{"w":"Thanks anyway. I will try to find another way.","p":"conj.","d":"anyway · 讓步","c":"還是謝謝你。我會想別的辦法。","s":"I am sorry, but I don't have any change for the bus. — That's all right, thanks anyway for stopping."},{"w":"anyway","p":"conj.","d":"anyway · 讓步","c":"無論如何／反正；用於轉回正題=anyway 也可用來拉回話題","s":"We talked about the movie for a long time. Anyway, back to our plan for the trip to Tainan."},{"w":"Anyway, let's stop here and talk about something else.","p":"conj.","d":"anyway · 語氣轉換","c":"總之，我們到此為止，聊點別的吧。","s":"Anyway, let's forget about the lost game and think about what to eat for lunch today."},{"w":"Anyway, what did you and your family do last weekend?","p":"conj.","d":"anyway · 語氣轉換","c":"話說回來，你和家人上週末做了什麼？","s":"Anyway, how was your trip to Japan last month, and did you see any beautiful flowers on the trees there?"},{"w":"Is there any way to fix it? — I don't know. Anyway, let's try.","p":"conj.","d":"anyway · 易混淆","c":"有什麼方法修好它嗎？——我不知道。反正，我們試試吧。","s":"I don't know any way to fix this old computer. Anyway, let's ask your uncle because he is good with machines."},{"w":"Don't be angry with him. After all, he is just a kid.","p":"conj.","d":"after all · 讓步","c":"別生他的氣。畢竟，他只是個小孩。","s":"Don't laugh at your little sister when she makes mistakes. After all, she is only learning to read."},{"w":"I thought I would fail, but I passed after all.","p":"conj.","d":"after all · 讓步","c":"我以為會不及格，但我終究還是通過了。","s":"We thought the bus would never come in the heavy rain, but it arrived after all, only ten minutes late."},{"w":"Let's eat here. After all, it's cheap and close.","p":"conj.","d":"after all · 讓步","c":"我們在這裡吃吧。畢竟又便宜又近。","s":"Let's buy Mom some flowers for her birthday. After all, she does so much for our family every day."},{"w":"after all (句首)","p":"conj.","d":"after all · 讓步","c":"畢竟；(句尾) = 終究還是=after all 位置不同意思不同","s":"I was worried about the math test all week, but it was not so hard after all."},{"w":"You don't have to worry. After all, it's just a game.","p":"conj.","d":"after all · 強調","c":"你不用擔心。畢竟，這只是場比賽。","s":"You don't need to feel bad about losing the game today. After all, you tried your best on the field."},{"w":"The test wasn't so bad after all.","p":"conj.","d":"after all · 強調","c":"考試結果並沒有那麼糟。","s":"It rained all morning, but the picnic was fun after all because the sun came out at noon."},{"w":"After all, he is your brother. / Above all, be kind. / All in all, it was fun.","p":"conj.","d":"after all · 易混淆","c":"畢竟他是你哥哥。／最重要的是，要善良。／總的來說，很有趣。","s":"All in all, the school trip was great, and after all, we got to spend a whole day with our friends."}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"in spite of – as (1)","cards":[{"w":"In spite of the rain, we had a great time at the beach.","p":"conj.","d":"in spite of · 讓步","c":"儘管下雨，我們在海邊玩得很開心。","s":"In spite of the strong wind and cold weather, many people came to the beach to watch the sun rise."},{"w":"He went to school in spite of his bad cold.","p":"conj.","d":"in spite of · 讓步","c":"儘管重感冒，他還是去上學。","s":"My grandmother still walks to the market every morning in spite of her bad knees and the hot sun."},{"w":"in spite of + N／V-ing（不接句子）","p":"conj.","d":"in spite of · 讓步","c":"in spite of 後面接名詞或動名詞","s":"In spite of studying hard for two weeks, Jack didn't do well on his English test and felt sad."},{"w":"No matter how hard it is, never give up.","p":"conj.","d":"no matter · 讓步","c":"不管多難，永遠不要放棄。","s":"No matter how busy my father is at work, he always comes home to have dinner with us."},{"w":"No matter what you say, I will go with you.","p":"conj.","d":"no matter · 讓步","c":"不管你說什麼，我都會跟你一起去。","s":"No matter what the weather is like tomorrow, our class will still go to the zoo by bus."},{"w":"No matter where you are, call me when you need help.","p":"conj.","d":"no matter · 讓步","c":"不管你在哪裡，需要幫忙時打給我。","s":"No matter where we travel this summer, I will bring my camera and take many pictures for you."},{"w":"no matter + wh- 疑問詞 (how / what / where / when / who)","p":"conj.","d":"no matter · 讓步","c":"no matter 後接疑問詞","s":"No matter who calls you tonight, don't answer the phone until you finish all of your homework."},{"w":"I stayed home because I had a bad cold.","p":"conj.","d":"because · 因果","c":"我待在家裡，因為我重感冒。","s":"Lisa missed the school bus this morning because she stayed up too late reading a comic book last night."},{"w":"Because it was late, we took a taxi home.","p":"conj.","d":"because · 因果","c":"因為很晚了，我們搭計程車回家。","s":"Because the restaurant was full of people on Friday night, we decided to buy pizza and eat at home."},{"w":"She was late because she missed the bus.","p":"conj.","d":"because · 因果","c":"她遲到了，因為她錯過公車。","s":"My little brother was crying in the living room because he lost his favorite toy car under the sofa."},{"w":"because + 句子；because 不與 so 連用","p":"conj.","d":"because · 因果","c":"because 後接句子，不可與 so 同時使用","s":"We didn't go hiking in the mountains last Sunday because the weather report said it would rain all day."},{"w":"The game was put off because of the heavy rain.","p":"conj.","d":"because of · 因果","c":"因為大雨，比賽延期了。","s":"The baseball game was put off until next week because of the heavy rain and strong wind yesterday."},{"w":"Because of the traffic, we got there an hour late.","p":"conj.","d":"because of · 因果","c":"因為塞車，我們晚了一小時才到。","s":"Because of the long line at the ticket window, we missed the first ten minutes of the movie."},{"w":"He is famous because of his beautiful songs.","p":"conj.","d":"because of · 因果","c":"他因為美妙的歌曲而出名。","s":"Many students love Mr. Lin's class because of his funny stories and the interesting games he plays with us."},{"w":"because of + N／V-ing（不接句子）","p":"conj.","d":"because of · 因果","c":"because of 後接名詞或動名詞","s":"Because of the traffic jam on the bridge this morning, my dad arrived at his office an hour late."},{"w":"Since you are here, why don't you join us for dinner?","p":"conj.","d":"since · 因果","c":"既然你來了，何不跟我們一起吃晚餐？","s":"Since it is such a beautiful sunny day, why don't we ride our bikes to the river and have a picnic?"},{"w":"Since it's your birthday, I will pay for the meal.","p":"conj.","d":"since · 因果","c":"既然是你的生日，這餐我請。","s":"Since you have already finished your homework, you can watch TV with your brother for half an hour."},{"w":"I have lived here since I was five years old.","p":"conj.","d":"since · 時間","c":"我從五歲起就住在這裡。","s":"My grandmother and grandfather have lived in the same old house in Tainan since they got married fifty years ago."},{"w":"She has been sick in bed since last Friday.","p":"conj.","d":"since · 時間","c":"她從上星期五開始就臥病在床。","s":"Tom has been a big fan of baseball since his father took him to his first game at the age of six."},{"w":"since + 過去時間點，主句用完成式","p":"conj.","d":"since · 時間","c":"since 主句用現在完成式","s":"Mary has studied English since she was in the third grade, so she speaks it very well now."},{"w":"He moved to Taipei in 2015 and has lived there ever since.","p":"conj.","d":"since · 其他用法","c":"他 2015 年搬到臺北，從那時起就一直住在那裡。","s":"My family moved to Taipei when I was seven, and we have lived in the same apartment ever since."},{"w":"I met her once last year. Since then, I haven't seen her.","p":"conj.","d":"since · 其他用法","c":"我去年見過她一次。從那之後就沒再見過她。","s":"Amy broke her leg while skating last winter, and since then she has been more careful when she exercises."},{"w":"since 當副詞：ever since / since then (從那時以來)","p":"conj.","d":"since · 其他用法","c":"since 副詞用法","s":"I ate too much ice cream at the party last year and got sick, and I have never eaten it since."},{"w":"She has been here since noon. / Since you are free, help me.","p":"conj.","d":"since · 易混淆","c":"她從中午就在這裡了。／既然你有空，幫我吧。","s":"Since you are not busy this afternoon, could you help me carry these books that have been here since morning?"},{"w":"As it was raining, we stayed inside and played cards.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 因果","c":"因為下雨，我們待在室內玩牌。","s":"As the weather was too hot to play outside, the children stayed in the living room and watched cartoons."},{"w":"I went to bed early, as I was very tired.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 因果","c":"我很早就睡了，因為我很累。","s":"Mom asked me to buy some eggs on the way home, as there were none left in the kitchen."},{"w":"as (因為) 語氣較弱；也可表「當…時」「如同」","p":"conj.","d":"as · 因果","c":"as 有「因為、當、如同」多種用法","s":"As it was my grandmother's birthday, the whole family went to her house for a big dinner on Sunday."},{"w":"As I was leaving the house, it started to rain.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 時間","c":"我正要離開家時，開始下雨了。","s":"As we were walking out of the movie theater, it suddenly started to rain very hard."},{"w":"As time goes by, you will understand your parents more.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 時間","c":"隨著時間過去，你會更了解你的父母。","s":"As the years go by, my grandfather's hair gets whiter, but his smile is still as warm as before."},{"w":"She sang as she walked along the river.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 時間","c":"她一邊沿著河走一邊唱歌。","s":"The little girl sang a happy song as she rode her bike along the quiet country road."},{"w":"as (當…時／一邊…一邊／隨著) 兩動作同時發生","p":"conj.","d":"as · 時間","c":"as 表兩個動作同時進行","s":"As the sun went down behind the mountains, the sky slowly turned from blue to orange and pink."},{"w":"Do as I say, not as I do.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"照我說的做，不要照我做的做。","s":"If you want to make good dumplings, just do as Grandma does and don't put too much water in."},{"w":"As you know, the test is next Monday.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"如你所知，考試在下星期一。","s":"As you know, the final exam is next week, so we should stop playing games and start to study."},{"w":"As usual, he was late for school again.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"一如往常，他上學又遲到了。","s":"As usual, my mother got up at six, made breakfast for everyone, and then drove us to school."},{"w":"As always, Mom cooked a big dinner for us.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"一如往常，媽媽為我們煮了一頓大餐。","s":"As always, Grandpa fell asleep in his favorite chair after lunch with the newspaper on his knees."},{"w":"as (如同、像…一樣) 表方式；as usual / as always / as you know","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"as 可表「如同、照著」","s":"As I said yesterday, we will meet at the train station at eight and then take the bus together."},{"w":"My mother works as a nurse in a big hospital.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"我媽媽在一家大醫院當護士。","s":"My aunt works as a cook in a small Japanese restaurant, and she makes the best noodles in town."},{"w":"As a child, I was afraid of dogs.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"小時候，我很怕狗。","s":"As a child, my father often went fishing with his grandfather in the river behind their old house."},{"w":"We used the big box as a table.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"我們把大箱子當桌子用。","s":"When we went camping last month, we used a big round stone as a table for our food."},{"w":"He went to the party dressed as a cat.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"他打扮成貓去參加派對。","s":"For the school party on Friday, my brother dressed as a lion, and everyone laughed when they saw him."}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"as (2) – therefore","cards":[{"w":"I will keep this picture as a gift from you.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"我會把這張照片當作你送的禮物收著。","s":"I will always keep this little bear as a gift from my best friend who moved to Japan last year."},{"w":"as 當介係詞","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"當作、作為、身為（work as / use A as B / dressed as）=as 介係詞表「當作、身為」","s":"My uncle has worked as a bus driver for twenty years, and he uses his free time as a chance to read."},{"w":"Tom is as tall as his father now.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"湯姆現在和他爸爸一樣高了。","s":"My little brother eats as much as my father now, so Mom has to cook more rice every night."},{"w":"This book is not as interesting as that one.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"這本書沒有那本有趣。","s":"The new game is not as interesting as the old one, so most of my friends stopped playing it quickly."},{"w":"She has as many books as I do.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"她的書和我一樣多。","s":"Lisa has as many stamps as her uncle, and she keeps them all in a big blue book."},{"w":"Eat as much fruit as you can.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"盡量多吃水果。","s":"Drink as much water as you can on hot days, or you may feel sick and tired after playing outside."},{"w":"The new room is twice as big as the old one.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"新房間是舊房間的兩倍大。","s":"Our new music room is twice as large as the old one, so there is much more space for our science projects."},{"w":"as + adj./adv. + as (和…一樣)；not as…as (不如)；倍數 + as…as","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"as…as 表同級比較","s":"Tom runs as fast as his older brother, but he is not as good as him at jumping."},{"w":"She can speak English as well as Japanese.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"她會說英文，也會說日文。","s":"My cousin can play the piano as well as the guitar, so she often plays music at family parties."},{"w":"As for me, I like tea better than coffee.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"至於我，我比較喜歡茶而不是咖啡。","s":"Everyone in my family likes to eat out on weekends, but as for me, I would rather cook at home."},{"w":"As far as I know, the store is closed today.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"就我所知，那家店今天沒開。","s":"As far as I know, the new swimming pool near the park will open to the public next month."},{"w":"The bag is as good as new after you cleaned it.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"你清理後，這個包包好得像新的一樣。","s":"After my father fixed the old bike and painted it red, it looked as good as new again."},{"w":"This is the same as mine.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"這個和我的一樣。","s":"The dress Mary wore to the party last night is the same as the one my sister bought last week."},{"w":"as 常見片語：as well as (也) / as for (至於) / as far as (就…而言) / as good as (幾乎) / the same as (和…相同) / such as (像) / as soon as (一…就) / as long as (只要) / as if (好像) / as a result (結果)","p":"conj.","d":"as · 其他用法","c":"as 片語整理","s":"As soon as the bell rang, the students ran out of the school as a result of the long test."},{"w":"As it is late, let's go home. / I was late because I missed the bus.","p":"conj.","d":"as · 易混淆","c":"既然很晚了，我們回家吧。／我遲到是因為錯過公車。","s":"As the store was closing soon, we hurried in, because we needed milk and eggs for breakfast tomorrow."},{"w":"It was hot, so we went swimming in the river.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 因果","c":"天氣很熱，所以我們去河裡游泳。","s":"It rained very hard all afternoon, so the baseball game was put off until next Saturday."},{"w":"I forgot my key, so I couldn't open the door.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 因果","c":"我忘了帶鑰匙，所以打不開門。","s":"My brother forgot to bring his lunch box to school, so I shared my sandwich and juice with him."},{"w":"He was sick, so he didn't come to school today.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 因果","c":"他生病了，所以今天沒來上學。","s":"Lisa stayed up late to watch a movie last night, so she fell asleep in math class this morning."},{"w":"…, so + 結果；so 不與 because 連用","p":"conj.","d":"so · 因果","c":"so 表結果，不可與 because 同時使用","s":"The weather was so nice this morning, so the whole family decided to have a picnic in the park."},{"w":"It is so cold today that I don't want to go out.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 其他用法","c":"今天好冷，我不想出門。","s":"The soup was so hot that my little brother had to wait ten minutes before he could drink it."},{"w":"I'm hungry. — So am I.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 其他用法","c":"我餓了。——我也是。","s":"I really love the new noodle shop near the school. — So do I, and the prices are low too."},{"w":"Will it rain tomorrow? — I think so.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 其他用法","c":"明天會下雨嗎？——我想會。","s":"Will Mr. Wang give us a quiz tomorrow? — I think so, because he told us to study hard."},{"w":"I have read five books so far this month.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 其他用法","c":"這個月到目前為止我讀了五本書。","s":"So far this year, our class has read eight English stories, and we hope to finish two more before summer."},{"w":"He said he was sick, and so he was.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 其他用法","c":"他說他病了，而他確實病了。","s":"My father said the old car would break down soon, and so it did on the highway last weekend."},{"w":"so + adj./adv. (如此) / So + 助動詞 + S (我也是) / think so, hope so, I'm afraid so / so far (到目前為止)","p":"conj.","d":"so · 其他用法","c":"so 的其他常見用法","s":"The movie was so exciting that nobody left their seats, and I hope so much to see it again."},{"w":"I like dogs. — So do I. / I don't like cats. — Neither do I.","p":"conj.","d":"so · 易混淆","c":"我喜歡狗。——我也是。／我不喜歡貓。——我也不喜歡。","s":"I don't like cold weather at all. — Neither do I, so let's stay inside and drink hot tea today."},{"w":"He didn't study. Therefore, he failed the test.","p":"conj.","d":"therefore · 因果","c":"他沒讀書。因此，他考不及格。","s":"Jack forgot to water the plants for two weeks. Therefore, most of the flowers in the garden died."},{"w":"It rained all week. Therefore, the river is high now.","p":"conj.","d":"therefore · 因果","c":"整週都在下雨。因此，河水現在很高。","s":"It snowed all night in the mountains. Therefore, the road to the village was closed this morning."},{"w":"The shop closed early. Therefore, we couldn't buy milk.","p":"conj.","d":"therefore · 因果","c":"商店很早關門。因此，我們買不到牛奶。","s":"Mary practiced the piano every day for a year. Therefore, she played very well at the school show."},{"w":"therefore, + 逗號（副詞，不能直接連接兩句）","p":"conj.","d":"therefore · 因果","c":"therefore 是副詞，前要句號或分號","s":"The bus was very late this morning. Therefore, many students missed the first class and the teacher was angry."}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"as a result – that's because","cards":[{"w":"She practiced every day. As a result, she won first prize.","p":"conj.","d":"as a result · 因果","c":"她每天練習。結果，她得了第一名。","s":"My brother ate three bowls of ice cream after dinner. As a result, he had a terrible stomachache all night."},{"w":"He ate too much. As a result, he got a stomachache.","p":"conj.","d":"as a result · 因果","c":"他吃太多。結果，他胃痛了。","s":"Tom didn't wear a coat on the cold windy day. As a result, he caught a bad cold and stayed home."},{"w":"It snowed heavily. As a result, all the schools were closed.","p":"conj.","d":"as a result · 因果","c":"下大雪。結果，所有學校都關閉了。","s":"It rained for five days without stopping. As a result, the river rose and many roads were under water."},{"w":"Speak louder so that everyone can hear you.","p":"conj.","d":"so that · 因果","c":"說大聲點，這樣大家才能聽到你。","s":"Please write your name clearly at the top of the paper so that the teacher knows whose test it is."},{"w":"I got up early so that I wouldn't miss the train.","p":"conj.","d":"so that · 因果","c":"我早起，這樣才不會錯過火車。","s":"My mother always gets up at five so that she can make a hot breakfast for us before school."},{"w":"She saved money so that she could buy a new bike.","p":"conj.","d":"so that · 因果","c":"她存錢，為了能買一台新腳踏車。","s":"We took a taxi to the station so that we would not miss the last train back to Taipei."},{"w":"so that + S + can／could／will／would（表目的）","p":"conj.","d":"so that · 因果","c":"so that 表目的，後常接 can/could","s":"Dad turned off the TV so that my sister could study for her big English test in a quiet room."},{"w":"The box was so heavy that I couldn't lift it.","p":"conj.","d":"so…that · 因果","c":"箱子重到我抬不起來。","s":"The wind was so strong last night that it blew down the big tree in front of our school."},{"w":"He was so tired that he fell asleep on the bus.","p":"conj.","d":"so…that · 因果","c":"他累到在公車上睡著了。","s":"My grandmother was so happy to see us that she cooked ten different dishes for dinner that night."},{"w":"The movie was so boring that many people left early.","p":"conj.","d":"so…that · 因果","c":"電影無聊到很多人提早離開。","s":"The math question was so difficult that even the teacher needed five minutes to find the right answer."},{"w":"so + adj.／adv. + that + 句子","p":"conj.","d":"so…that · 因果","c":"so 後接形容詞或副詞","s":"Lisa ran so fast in the race that nobody in the school could catch up with her at all."},{"w":"It was such a hot day that we stayed inside.","p":"conj.","d":"such…that · 因果","c":"天氣熱到我們都待在室內。","s":"It was such a cold morning that my mother made us wear two sweaters and thick gloves to school."},{"w":"She is such a kind girl that everyone likes her.","p":"conj.","d":"such…that · 因果","c":"她是個如此善良的女孩，大家都喜歡她。","s":"Mr. Chen is such a funny teacher that students never fall asleep in his history class after lunch."},{"w":"They made such a big noise that the baby woke up.","p":"conj.","d":"such…that · 因果","c":"他們製造很大的噪音，把寶寶吵醒了。","s":"The children made the kitchen such a dirty place that Mom spent the whole afternoon cleaning it up."},{"w":"such + (a／an) + adj. + N + that","p":"conj.","d":"such…that · 因果","c":"such 後接名詞片語","s":"It was such heavy rain this afternoon that all the students had to stay inside the school for an hour."},{"w":"I went to bed early, for I was very tired.","p":"conj.","d":"for · 因果","c":"我早早上床，因為我很累。","s":"Lily put on her warm coat before she left home, for the wind was cold and strong this morning."},{"w":"She must be sick, for she looks pale today.","p":"conj.","d":"for · 因果","c":"她一定是病了，因為她今天臉色蒼白。","s":"Tom did not come to school today, for he had a bad cold and a high fever last night."},{"w":"for (因為) 屬 FANBOYS，前加逗號，不放句首","p":"conj.","d":"for · 因果","c":"for 作連接詞時前面加逗號","s":"My mother went to bed early last night, for she had to get up at five this morning."},{"w":"We waited for the bus for twenty minutes.","p":"conj.","d":"for · 其他用法","c":"我們等公車等了二十分鐘。","s":"We have lived in this small town near the sea for ten years, and we love it very much."},{"w":"This gift is for you. Happy birthday!","p":"conj.","d":"for · 其他用法","c":"這個禮物是給你的。生日快樂！","s":"This beautiful card is for you, Grandma, and my little brother made the red flowers on it."},{"w":"The old house is for sale now.","p":"conj.","d":"for · 其他用法","c":"這間老房子現在要出售。","s":"The blue bike in front of the store is for sale, and it costs only two thousand dollars."},{"w":"I'm sorry for being late again.","p":"conj.","d":"for · 其他用法","c":"很抱歉我又遲到了。","s":"I am really sorry for breaking your favorite cup, so I will buy you a new one tomorrow."},{"w":"What is this little button for?","p":"conj.","d":"for · 其他用法","c":"這個小按鈕是做什麼用的？","s":"What is this long black box in the kitchen for, and why does Dad keep it near the window?"},{"w":"for 當介係詞：for + 一段時間 (持續) / for sb. (給) / for sale (出售) / sorry for / What…for? (做什麼用)","p":"conj.","d":"for · 其他用法","c":"for 介係詞常見用法","s":"We waited for the train for thirty minutes, and then Mom bought a hot drink for me."},{"w":"I stayed home, for it was raining. / Because it was raining, I stayed home.","p":"conj.","d":"for · 易混淆","c":"我待在家，因為下雨了。／因為下雨，我待在家。","s":"I stayed at home all day, for it was raining hard and the streets were full of water."},{"w":"He never does his homework. That's why the teacher is angry.","p":"conj.","d":"that's why · 因果","c":"他從不寫作業。那就是老師生氣的原因。","s":"Peter stayed up late playing computer games, and that's why he fell asleep in math class today."},{"w":"It rained a lot. That's why the road is wet.","p":"conj.","d":"that's why · 因果","c":"下了很多雨。那就是路濕的原因。","s":"My sister practices the piano for two hours every day, and that's why she plays so well now."},{"w":"The road is wet. That's because it rained last night.","p":"conj.","d":"that's because · 因果","c":"路是濕的。那是因為昨晚下雨了。","s":"Amy did not eat anything at lunch, and that's because she had a terrible stomachache this morning."},{"w":"She looks happy. That's because she passed the test.","p":"conj.","d":"that's because · 因果","c":"她看起來很開心。那是因為她通過了考試。","s":"The whole class was very quiet today, and that's because the teacher was giving a big test."}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"now that – nor","cards":[{"w":"Now that you are eighteen, you can drive a car.","p":"conj.","d":"now that · 因果","c":"既然你十八歲了，你可以開車了。","s":"Now that you have finished all your homework, you can watch TV with your little brother."},{"w":"Now that the rain has stopped, let's go out.","p":"conj.","d":"now that · 因果","c":"既然雨停了，我們出去吧。","s":"Now that the weather is getting warmer, many families go to the beach on Sunday afternoons."},{"w":"Thanks to your help, I finished the work on time.","p":"conj.","d":"thanks to · 因果","c":"多虧你的幫忙，我準時完成了工作。","s":"Thanks to my kind neighbor, my little dog found its way home safely last night."},{"w":"Thanks to the map, we didn't get lost in the city.","p":"conj.","d":"thanks to · 因果","c":"多虧有地圖，我們沒在城裡迷路。","s":"Thanks to the new bridge, people in the village can now get to the city in twenty minutes."},{"w":"thanks to + N（多虧…，常用於好的結果）","p":"conj.","d":"thanks to · 因果","c":"thanks to 多用於正面結果","s":"Thanks to the rain last week, the farmers will have a lot of rice and vegetables this year."},{"w":"Thanks to your help, we won. / Thank you for your help. / Thanks for coming.","p":"conj.","d":"thanks to · 易混淆","c":"多虧你的幫忙我們贏了。／謝謝你的幫忙。／謝謝你來。","s":"Thanks to my English teacher, I am not afraid to talk with people from other countries now."},{"w":"I bought some apples and oranges at the market.","p":"conj.","d":"and · 附加","c":"我在市場買了一些蘋果和橘子。","s":"My mother bought some fish, eggs, and fresh vegetables at the market this morning for dinner."},{"w":"Work hard, and you will pass the test.","p":"conj.","d":"and · 附加","c":"努力讀書，你就會通過考試。","s":"Get up early tomorrow, and you will see the beautiful sun come up over the sea."},{"w":"She opened the door and walked into the room.","p":"conj.","d":"and · 附加","c":"她打開門走進房間。","s":"After school, Jack went home, washed his hands, and had a big bowl of noodles with his family."},{"w":"命令句 + and","p":"conj.","d":"and · 附加","c":"如果…就…（if 的意思）=命令句後接 and 表「如果就」","s":"Eat more vegetables and drink more water, and you will feel much healthier in a few weeks."},{"w":"We bought apples, bananas, oranges, and so on.","p":"conj.","d":"and · 其他用法","c":"我們買了蘋果、香蕉、橘子等等。","s":"For the picnic, we need to bring sandwiches, fruit, cold drinks, paper cups, and so on."},{"w":"Come and see what I found in the garden!","p":"conj.","d":"and · 其他用法","c":"來看看我在花園發現了什麼！","s":"Come and see the baby birds in the tree outside my window before they fly away!"},{"w":"The weather is getting hotter and hotter.","p":"conj.","d":"and · 其他用法","c":"天氣越來越熱了。","s":"The days are getting shorter and shorter, and the nights are colder in late November."},{"w":"I tried again and again, but I still failed.","p":"conj.","d":"and · 其他用法","c":"我一次又一次嘗試，但還是失敗了。","s":"My little brother asked the same question again and again until Mom finally gave him an answer."},{"w":"Both Tom and Mary like to play basketball.","p":"conj.","d":"and · 其他用法","c":"湯姆和瑪麗都喜歡打籃球。","s":"Both my cousin and I love swimming, so we go to the pool together every Saturday morning."},{"w":"and so on (等等) / come and see","p":"conj.","d":"and · 其他用法","c":"come to see / 比較級 and 比較級 (越來越) / again and again (一再) / both A and B=and 的片語整理","s":"Come and see how the river is getting higher and higher after the heavy rain this week!"},{"w":"Hurry up, or you will miss the school bus.","p":"conj.","d":"or · 條件","c":"快點，否則你會錯過校車。","s":"Finish your dinner quickly, or you will be late for your piano lesson at seven o'clock."},{"w":"Do you want tea or coffee after dinner?","p":"conj.","d":"or · 條件","c":"晚餐後你想喝茶還是咖啡？","s":"Do you want to walk to the museum or take the bus with us this afternoon?"},{"w":"Put on your coat, or you will catch a cold.","p":"conj.","d":"or · 條件","c":"穿上外套，否則你會感冒。","s":"Hold my hand when we cross the busy street, or a car may hit you."},{"w":"命令句 + or","p":"conj.","d":"or · 條件","c":"否則（= otherwise）=命令句後接 or 表「否則」","s":"Study hard for the test this week, or you will have to take it again next month."},{"w":"There were twenty or so people at the party.","p":"conj.","d":"or · 其他用法","c":"派對上大約有二十個人。","s":"There were fifty or so students in the school library this afternoon because of the big test."},{"w":"Hurry up, or else we will miss the train.","p":"conj.","d":"or · 其他用法","c":"快點，不然我們會錯過火車。","s":"We have to leave for the airport now, or else we will miss our plane to Japan."},{"w":"Would you like tea, coffee, or juice?","p":"conj.","d":"or · 其他用法","c":"你想喝茶、咖啡還是果汁？","s":"Would you like to have rice, noodles, or bread for breakfast tomorrow morning before you go to school?"},{"w":"I don't like fish or chicken.","p":"conj.","d":"or · 其他用法","c":"我不喜歡魚，也不喜歡雞肉。","s":"My little sister does not like milk or cheese, so Mom gives her juice with breakfast every day."},{"w":"or so (大約) / or else (否則) / 否定句中的 or","p":"conj.","d":"or · 其他用法","c":"也不 (not A or B)=or 的其他用法","s":"There were thirty or so people at the bus stop, so hurry up, or else we won't get a seat."},{"w":"He doesn't like fish, nor does he like chicken.","p":"conj.","d":"nor · 附加","c":"他不喜歡魚，也不喜歡雞肉。","s":"My father does not drink coffee, nor does he drink tea, so he always orders water."},{"w":"I have never been to Japan, nor has my sister.","p":"conj.","d":"nor · 附加","c":"我從沒去過日本，我妹妹也沒有。","s":"Mary has never seen snow in her life, nor have her parents, because they live in the south."},{"w":"nor + 助動詞 + 主詞（倒裝）","p":"conj.","d":"nor · 附加","c":"nor 後面要倒裝","s":"I cannot play the guitar, nor can my brother, so we just sing together at parties."}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"also – as well","cards":[{"w":"She can sing well. She can also dance beautifully.","p":"conj.","d":"also · 附加","c":"她歌唱得好。她也跳舞跳得很美。","s":"Kevin is good at basketball, and he is also the best runner in our whole school."},{"w":"I like pizza. My brother also likes it a lot.","p":"conj.","d":"also · 附加","c":"我喜歡披薩。我哥哥也很喜歡。","s":"My grandmother cooks delicious food, and she also makes beautiful dresses for all the girls in our family."},{"w":"also 放在 be 動詞後、一般動詞前","p":"conj.","d":"also · 附加","c":"also 的位置在動詞前或 be 動詞後","s":"Our teacher is also a great singer, and she also plays the guitar for us on Friday afternoons."},{"w":"I love ice cream. My little sister loves it, too.","p":"conj.","d":"too · 附加","c":"我愛冰淇淋。我妹妹也愛。","s":"I love the new ice cream shop near the school, and my best friend loves it, too."},{"w":"He is a good student, and he is a good player, too.","p":"conj.","d":"too · 附加","c":"他是好學生，也是好球員。","s":"Jenny can speak Japanese very well, and her younger brother can speak it quite well, too."},{"w":"too 放句尾（肯定句），前加逗號；否定句用 either","p":"conj.","d":"too · 附加","c":"too 用於肯定句句尾","s":"My father enjoys fishing by the river on weekends, and my uncle enjoys it very much, too."},{"w":"The box is too heavy for me to carry.","p":"conj.","d":"too · 其他用法","c":"這箱子太重，我搬不動。","s":"This math problem is too hard for me to finish alone, so could you help me?"},{"w":"It is never too late to learn.","p":"conj.","d":"too · 其他用法","c":"學習永遠不嫌晚。","s":"Grandpa says it is never too late to learn, so he started English lessons at seventy."},{"w":"Don't eat too much candy before dinner.","p":"conj.","d":"too · 其他用法","c":"晚餐前別吃太多糖。","s":"Don't drink too much cold water after you run, or you may get a stomachache."},{"w":"I like it, too. — Me too!","p":"conj.","d":"too · 其他用法","c":"我也喜歡。——我也是！","s":"When I said I wanted pizza for dinner, my little brother shouted, Me too, from his room."},{"w":"too + adj. + to V (太…而不能) / too much + 不可數 N / too many + 複數 N / Me too (我也是)","p":"conj.","d":"too · 其他用法","c":"too 表「太」的句型","s":"There are too many people and too much noise in the night market, so it is too hot to stay."},{"w":"The coffee is too hot to drink. / The coffee is very hot. / The coffee is so hot that I can't drink it.","p":"conj.","d":"too · 易混淆","c":"咖啡太熱不能喝。／咖啡非常熱。／咖啡熱到我不能喝。","s":"The bag is too heavy for me to carry, so my very strong brother carries it for me."},{"w":"I don't like math. My brother doesn't like it, either.","p":"conj.","d":"either · 附加","c":"我不喜歡數學。我弟弟也不喜歡。","s":"I don't like getting up early on Sundays, and my sister doesn't like it, either."},{"w":"She can't swim, and I can't swim, either.","p":"conj.","d":"either · 附加","c":"她不會游泳，我也不會。","s":"Tom can't come to the party tonight, and his cousin Jack can't come to it, either."},{"w":"either 放否定句句尾；肯定句用 too","p":"conj.","d":"either · 附加","c":"either 用於否定句句尾","s":"My mom doesn't eat any meat, and my dad doesn't eat it very often, either."},{"w":"You can sit on either side of the table.","p":"conj.","d":"either · 其他用法","c":"你可以坐在桌子的任何一邊。","s":"You can put your bag on either side of the desk, because both sides are empty."},{"w":"Either of the two books is fine with me.","p":"conj.","d":"either · 其他用法","c":"這兩本書中任一本我都可以。","s":"Either of these two red dresses looks great on you, so just pick the one you like."},{"w":"There are trees on either side of the road.","p":"conj.","d":"either · 其他用法","c":"路的兩旁都有樹。","s":"There were tall trees on either side of the road, so the walk to school was cool."},{"w":"I don't like either of them.","p":"conj.","d":"either · 其他用法","c":"他們兩個我都不喜歡。","s":"Mom showed me two shirts at the store, but I didn't like either of them very much."},{"w":"either (兩者之一／兩邊都) + 單數名詞；either of + 複數","p":"conj.","d":"either · 其他用法","c":"either 當形容詞／代名詞","s":"Either answer is fine for this question, and either of the two students may explain it."},{"w":"I can swim, too. / I can't swim, either. / Neither of us can swim.","p":"conj.","d":"either · 易混淆","c":"我也會游泳。／我也不會游泳。／我們兩個都不會游泳。","s":"Lisa can't ride a bike yet, and her little brother can't ride one, either, so they walk."},{"w":"I bought a hat, and I bought some shoes as well.","p":"conj.","d":"as well · 附加","c":"我買了一頂帽子，也買了一些鞋子。","s":"We visited the old temple in the morning, and we saw the famous night market as well."},{"w":"He speaks English well, and he speaks Japanese as well.","p":"conj.","d":"as well · 附加","c":"他英文說得好，日文也說得好。","s":"My aunt speaks English and Japanese, and she is learning a little French as well."},{"w":"as well","p":"conj.","d":"as well · 附加","c":"too，放句尾，不加逗號=as well 等於 too","s":"Lucy bought a birthday cake for her mom, and she bought some pretty flowers as well."},{"w":"She can speak English as well as French.","p":"conj.","d":"as well · 其他用法","c":"她會說英文，也會說法文。","s":"My brother can cook Chinese food as well as Italian food, so dinner is always exciting."},{"w":"The teacher, as well as the students, was happy about the trip.","p":"conj.","d":"as well · 其他用法","c":"老師和學生們都對這次旅行感到高興。","s":"The teacher, as well as her students, was excited about the trip to the zoo."},{"w":"It's raining. We may as well stay home and watch TV.","p":"conj.","d":"as well · 其他用法","c":"在下雨。我們不妨待在家看電視。","s":"It is too cold to go out tonight, so we may as well stay home and make hot soup."},{"w":"as well as (以及，","p":"conj.","d":"as well · 其他用法","c":"and；動詞與前者一致) / may as well (不妨) / as well (也，句尾)=as well 的片語整理","s":"Tom plays the piano as well as the guitar, and he sings in the school band as well."}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"besides – such as","cards":[{"w":"I don't want to go out. Besides, it's raining now.","p":"conj.","d":"besides · 附加","c":"我不想出門。此外，現在正在下雨。","s":"I don't want to go swimming today, and besides, the water in the pool is too cold."},{"w":"The hotel is too far. Besides, it costs too much.","p":"conj.","d":"besides · 附加","c":"飯店太遠了。此外，太貴了。","s":"We should not buy that old car, and besides, we don't have enough money this month."},{"w":"Besides English, she can also speak Japanese and a little French.","p":"conj.","d":"besides · 附加","c":"除了英文之外，她還會說日文和一點法文。","s":"Besides pizza, the new restaurant near our school also sells delicious noodles and fresh salad."},{"w":"Besides English, she speaks French. / She sat beside me. / Everyone came except Tom.","p":"conj.","d":"besides · 易混淆","c":"除了英文她還會說法文。／她坐在我旁邊。／除了湯姆大家都來了。","s":"It is late and dark now, and besides, the last bus has already left the station."},{"w":"The food was great. What's more, it was very cheap.","p":"conj.","d":"what's more · 附加","c":"食物很棒。更棒的是，非常便宜。","s":"The new teacher is very kind, and what's more, she makes every English class fun for us."},{"w":"He is smart. What's more, he is always kind to others.","p":"conj.","d":"what's more · 附加","c":"他很聰明。更重要的是，他總是對人很好。","s":"This phone is cheap and light, and what's more, it takes very clear pictures at night."},{"w":"She works at a bank. In addition, she teaches English at night.","p":"conj.","d":"in addition · 附加","c":"她在銀行工作。此外，她晚上教英文。","s":"My mother teaches music at a high school, and in addition, she sings in a church group on Sundays."},{"w":"The car is fast. In addition, it is easy to drive.","p":"conj.","d":"in addition · 附加","c":"這輛車很快。此外，它很好開。","s":"The hotel room was clean and big, and in addition, the breakfast there was really delicious."},{"w":"The book is interesting. Moreover, it is easy to read.","p":"conj.","d":"moreover · 附加","c":"這本書很有趣。而且，很容易讀。","s":"The library is close to my house, and moreover, it is open until nine every night."},{"w":"It is late. Moreover, I don't have any money with me.","p":"conj.","d":"moreover · 附加","c":"很晚了。而且，我身上沒錢。","s":"Peter is a good basketball player, and moreover, he gets good grades in every subject at school."},{"w":"This phone is cheap. Furthermore, it takes great pictures.","p":"conj.","d":"furthermore · 附加","c":"這手機很便宜。而且，拍照很棒。","s":"The park near our school is clean and quiet, and furthermore, it has a big pool for kids."},{"w":"The park is close to home. Furthermore, it is free.","p":"conj.","d":"furthermore · 附加","c":"公園離家很近。而且，是免費的。","s":"This restaurant serves delicious food at a low price, and furthermore, the waiters are always friendly."},{"w":"She is not only smart but also very kind.","p":"conj.","d":"not only…but also · 附加","c":"她不但聰明，而且很善良。","s":"My grandmother not only cooks the best dumplings but also tells the funniest stories at dinner."},{"w":"He can not only sing but also play the piano.","p":"conj.","d":"not only…but also · 附加","c":"他不但會唱歌，而且會彈鋼琴。","s":"The new shopping center is not only big but also very close to the train station."},{"w":"Not only the kids but also their parents love the show.","p":"conj.","d":"not only…but also · 附加","c":"不只孩子，連他們的父母也愛這個節目。","s":"Not only the students but also their teacher was surprised by the big snow this morning."},{"w":"not only A but also B；動詞與 B 一致（就近原則）","p":"conj.","d":"not only…but also · 附加","c":"動詞配合靠近的主詞 B","s":"Not only my parents but also my little sister enjoys watching old movies on Saturday nights."},{"w":"Both my father and my mother are teachers.","p":"conj.","d":"both…and · 附加","c":"我爸爸和媽媽都是老師。","s":"Both my grandfather and my grandmother get up at five every morning to exercise in the park."},{"w":"She likes both reading books and swimming in the sea.","p":"conj.","d":"both…and · 附加","c":"她喜歡看書和在海裡游泳兩者。","s":"Amy enjoys both playing basketball with her friends and reading quietly in her room on weekends."},{"w":"both A and B + 複數動詞","p":"conj.","d":"both…and · 附加","c":"both…and 接複數動詞","s":"Both the teacher and the students were tired after the long school trip to the mountains."},{"w":"I like sports outside. For example, I often go hiking with friends.","p":"conj.","d":"for example · 舉例","c":"我喜歡戶外運動。例如，我常和朋友去爬山。","s":"Many students in my class love sports, and for example, Tom plays basketball every day after school."},{"w":"Many animals sleep in winter. Bears, for example, sleep for months.","p":"conj.","d":"for example · 舉例","c":"很多動物冬天睡覺。例如，熊會睡好幾個月。","s":"Some animals, for example, cats and dogs, can hear sounds that people cannot hear at all."},{"w":"You should eat more fruit, for example, apples and bananas.","p":"conj.","d":"for example · 舉例","c":"你應該多吃水果，例如蘋果和香蕉。","s":"You should learn some simple Japanese words before the trip, for example, hello and thank you."},{"w":"Some fruits are sour. For instance, lemons are very sour.","p":"conj.","d":"for instance · 舉例","c":"有些水果是酸的。例如，檸檬很酸。","s":"My brother is very good at fixing things, and for instance, he fixed my old bike yesterday."},{"w":"She is good at sports. For instance, she runs very fast.","p":"conj.","d":"for instance · 舉例","c":"她擅長運動。例如，她跑得很快。","s":"Some fruits, for instance, bananas and apples, are easy to carry to school for a snack."},{"w":"I love fruits such as apples, bananas, and grapes.","p":"conj.","d":"such as · 舉例","c":"我喜歡水果，像蘋果、香蕉和葡萄。","s":"On hot summer days, I like cold drinks such as juice, iced tea, and lemon water."},{"w":"We visited many places, such as Taipei and Tainan.","p":"conj.","d":"such as · 舉例","c":"我們去了很多地方，像臺北和臺南。","s":"Our teacher asked us to bring things such as paper, crayons, and old magazines for art class."},{"w":"such as + N（舉例），不接句子","p":"conj.","d":"such as · 舉例","c":"such as 後面接名詞","s":"Taiwan has many beautiful places such as Sun Moon Lake and Taroko, so visitors come every year."},{"w":"such + (a/an) + adj. + N (如此…的) / such as (像…) / as such (本身)","p":"conj.","d":"such as · 其他用法","c":"such 的其他用法","s":"Tom is such a good cook that he can make dishes such as beef noodles and fried rice."}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"like – first","cards":[{"w":"I enjoy sweet food like cake and ice cream.","p":"conj.","d":"like · 舉例","c":"我喜歡甜食，像蛋糕和冰淇淋。","s":"My little cousin loves sweet drinks like milk tea and juice, but Mom says they are bad for teeth."},{"w":"Big cities like Taipei are often very crowded.","p":"conj.","d":"like · 舉例","c":"像臺北這樣的大城市常常很擠。","s":"Small animals like rabbits and birds get scared easily, so please stay quiet near them at the farm."},{"w":"like (像…一樣，介係詞) ≠ like (喜歡，動詞)","p":"conj.","d":"like · 舉例","c":"like 可作介係詞表「像」","s":"Children like my little brother like to play outside after dinner, so the park is always busy."},{"w":"I like to read before I go to bed.","p":"conj.","d":"like · 其他用法","c":"我喜歡在睡前閱讀。","s":"I like to listen to music while I do my homework, but my mother thinks it is noisy."},{"w":"Would you like some tea or coffee?","p":"conj.","d":"like · 其他用法","c":"你想要喝茶還是咖啡？","s":"Would you like some hot soup and bread for lunch, or do you want noodles instead?"},{"w":"I don't feel like going out tonight.","p":"conj.","d":"like · 其他用法","c":"我今晚不想出門。","s":"I don't feel like going to the movies tonight because I am very tired after basketball practice."},{"w":"What is your new teacher like?","p":"conj.","d":"like · 其他用法","c":"你的新老師是怎樣的人？","s":"What is your new English teacher like, and does she give a lot of homework every week?"},{"w":"She looks like her mother when she smiles.","p":"conj.","d":"like · 其他用法","c":"她微笑時看起來像她媽媽。","s":"My baby sister looks like our father when she laughs, but she has our mother's big eyes."},{"w":"It looks like rain. Take an umbrella.","p":"conj.","d":"like · 其他用法","c":"看起來要下雨了。帶把傘。","s":"It looks like rain this afternoon, so you had better take an umbrella to school with you."},{"w":"like 當動詞 (喜歡) / would like (想要) / feel like + V-ing (想要做) / look like (看起來像) / What is…like? (…是怎樣的)","p":"conj.","d":"like · 其他用法","c":"like 動詞與片語整理","s":"I would like to try new food like Thai dishes, and I feel like eating out tonight."},{"w":"He swims like a fish. / Do as I say. / The two sisters look alike.","p":"conj.","d":"like · 易混淆","c":"他游泳像魚一樣。／照我說的做。／這兩姊妹看起來很像。","s":"My uncle swims like a fish in the sea, so everyone at the beach watches him with surprise."},{"w":"She left early, that is, before the party ended.","p":"conj.","d":"that is · 舉例","c":"她提早離開了，也就是說，在派對結束前。","s":"Our school starts very early, that is, at seven thirty, so I have to get up at six."},{"w":"He only eats vegetables. That is, he never eats any meat.","p":"conj.","d":"that is · 舉例","c":"他只吃蔬菜。也就是說，他從不吃肉。","s":"My grandfather is a farmer, that is, he grows rice and vegetables in the fields near our town."},{"w":"that is (to say)","p":"conj.","d":"that is · 舉例","c":"也就是說，用來說明前句=that is 用來進一步解釋","s":"Lily never eats meat or fish, that is to say, she only eats vegetables, fruit, rice, and eggs."},{"w":"He didn't call. In other words, he isn't coming tonight.","p":"conj.","d":"in other words · 總結","c":"他沒打電話。換句話說，他今晚不來了。","s":"The teacher said the test was not easy, and in other words, we need to study much harder."},{"w":"The shop is closed. In other words, we can't buy anything now.","p":"conj.","d":"in other words · 總結","c":"商店關了。換句話說，我們現在買不到東西。","s":"Dad said he was too busy this weekend, and in other words, we are not going to the zoo."},{"w":"First of all, wash your hands before you eat.","p":"conj.","d":"first of all · 順序","c":"首先，吃飯前先洗手。","s":"First of all, please turn off your phones, and then we can begin the English class quietly."},{"w":"First of all, let me thank everyone for coming today.","p":"conj.","d":"first of all · 順序","c":"首先，讓我感謝大家今天的到來。","s":"First of all, I want to thank my parents, because they always help me when I have problems."},{"w":"first of all (句首)","p":"conj.","d":"first of all · 順序","c":"首先；之後常接 second / then / finally=first of all 常與 then、finally 搭配","s":"First of all, wash the rice, then put it in the pot, and finally cook it for twenty minutes."},{"w":"To begin with, we need to buy some eggs and milk.","p":"conj.","d":"to begin with · 順序","c":"首先，我們需要買一些蛋和牛奶。","s":"To begin with, we need to clean the room, and after that we can hang the colorful paper for the party."},{"w":"To begin with, the hotel was dirty. Then the food was bad.","p":"conj.","d":"to begin with · 順序","c":"首先，飯店很髒。接著，食物又很難吃。","s":"To begin with, the hotel was far from the beach, and then the food there was cold and expensive."},{"w":"First, mix the eggs and sugar. Then, add some milk.","p":"conj.","d":"first · 順序","c":"首先，把蛋和糖混合。然後，加一些牛奶。","s":"First, boil some water in a big pot, and then put the noodles in for three minutes."},{"w":"First, turn off the light. Next, lock the door.","p":"conj.","d":"first · 順序","c":"首先，關燈。接著，鎖門。","s":"First, write your name at the top of the paper, and next, read all the questions carefully."},{"w":"This is my first time to visit Japan.","p":"conj.","d":"first · 其他用法","c":"這是我第一次去日本。","s":"This is my first time to ride a train by myself, so I feel a little nervous today."},{"w":"He fell in love with her at first sight.","p":"conj.","d":"first · 其他用法","c":"他對她一見鍾情。","s":"My parents fell in love at first sight at a friend's birthday party twenty years ago."},{"w":"In our family, safety always comes first.","p":"conj.","d":"first · 其他用法","c":"在我們家，安全永遠第一。","s":"In our family, homework always comes first, so I cannot play games before I finish it."},{"w":"Who came in first in the race?","p":"conj.","d":"first · 其他用法","c":"賽跑中誰第一個到達？","s":"Who came in first in the swimming race this morning, Tom or his best friend Kevin?"},{"w":"first 當形容詞 (第一的) / 副詞 (最先)；first time (第一次) / at first sight (第一眼) / come first (居首／最重要)","p":"conj.","d":"first · 其他用法","c":"first 的其他用法","s":"Mary won first prize for her first painting, and her teacher says art always comes first for her."},{"w":"First, cut the apple. / At first I didn't like him, but now we are friends.","p":"conj.","d":"first · 易混淆","c":"首先切蘋果。／起初我不喜歡他，但現在我們是朋友。","s":"First, read the story quietly, and at first you may not understand everything, but keep going."}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"second – later","cards":[{"w":"First, he is kind. Second, he is always on time.","p":"conj.","d":"second · 順序","c":"第一，他很善良。第二，他總是準時。","s":"First, you should drink more water every day, and second, you should go to bed before eleven."},{"w":"Second, read the questions carefully before you answer.","p":"conj.","d":"second · 順序","c":"第二，回答前仔細讀題目。","s":"Second, check your answers one more time before you give the test paper to the teacher."},{"w":"Wait a second. I'm almost ready.","p":"conj.","d":"second · 其他用法","c":"等一下。我快好了。","s":"Wait a second, Mom, I just need to find my other shoe before we leave for school."},{"w":"I bought a second-hand bike for only five hundred dollars.","p":"conj.","d":"second · 其他用法","c":"我只花五百元買了一台二手腳踏車。","s":"My father bought a second-hand car last month, and it still runs very well on long trips."},{"w":"On second thought, let's take the bus instead.","p":"conj.","d":"second · 其他用法","c":"再想一想，我們還是搭公車吧。","s":"On second thought, let's eat at home tonight, because the restaurants are too full of people on weekends."},{"w":"She finished second in the 100-meter race.","p":"conj.","d":"second · 其他用法","c":"她在一百公尺賽跑中得第二。","s":"Jenny finished second in the running race, so she was very proud and her parents took many pictures."},{"w":"second 當名詞 (秒／一下子) / 形容詞 (第二的)；second-hand (二手的) / on second thought (再想想) / every second day (每隔一天)","p":"conj.","d":"second · 其他用法","c":"second 的其他用法","s":"Wait a second, because on second thought I want to buy that second-hand bike after all."},{"w":"We had dinner, and then we watched a movie together.","p":"conj.","d":"then · 順序","c":"我們吃了晚餐，然後一起看電影。","s":"We finished our homework at the library, and then we went to the night market for some snacks."},{"w":"Turn left at the bank. Then you will see the park.","p":"conj.","d":"then · 順序","c":"在銀行左轉。然後你就會看到公園。","s":"Walk straight for two blocks and turn right at the bank, and then you will see the post office."},{"w":"If you are not busy, then come and help me.","p":"conj.","d":"then · 順序","c":"如果你不忙，那就來幫我。","s":"If you don't like this red shirt, then try the blue one, because it looks nice on you."},{"w":"then","p":"conj.","d":"then · 順序","c":"然後（時間）；then = 那麼（if 的結果）=then 有「然後」和「那麼」兩義","s":"If it rains tomorrow, then we will stay home, cook lunch together, and then watch a movie."},{"w":"Back then, there were no cellphones at all.","p":"conj.","d":"then · 其他用法","c":"那時候，根本沒有手機。","s":"Back then, my grandmother and grandfather had no TV at home, so they listened to the radio every night."},{"w":"Finish your homework by then, or you can't watch TV.","p":"conj.","d":"then · 其他用法","c":"在那之前寫完作業，否則不能看電視。","s":"The bus leaves at eight, so please finish your breakfast by then and bring your school bag."},{"w":"We still meet now and then for coffee.","p":"conj.","d":"then · 其他用法","c":"我們現在仍偶爾見面喝咖啡。","s":"My old friends from school and I still meet now and then at a small coffee shop near our school."},{"w":"I was only five then, so I don't remember much.","p":"conj.","d":"then · 其他用法","c":"我那時才五歲，所以記不太清楚。","s":"My family moved to Taipei ten years ago, and I was only four years old then."},{"w":"then 當副詞","p":"conj.","d":"then · 其他用法","c":"那時：back then / by then / since then / now and then (偶爾) / just then (就在那時)=then 表「那時」的片語","s":"Back then, we had no computers at school, and since then many things have changed a lot."},{"w":"First, cut the apples. Next, put them in the bowl.","p":"conj.","d":"next · 順序","c":"首先，切蘋果。接著，把它們放進碗裡。","s":"First, put the eggs in the bowl, and next, add some sugar and milk and mix them well."},{"w":"Next, write your name on the top of the paper.","p":"conj.","d":"next · 順序","c":"接著，在紙的上方寫上你的名字。","s":"Next, open your books to page ten and read the short story about the lost cat quietly."},{"w":"The bookstore is next to the bank.","p":"conj.","d":"next · 其他用法","c":"書店在銀行旁邊。","s":"The new bookstore is next to the post office, so you can buy stamps and comic books together."},{"w":"My best friend lives next door to me.","p":"conj.","d":"next · 其他用法","c":"我最好的朋友住在我隔壁。","s":"An old lady lives next door to us, and she often gives us cookies that she makes herself."},{"w":"The next day, we went to the beach again.","p":"conj.","d":"next · 其他用法","c":"第二天，我們又去了海邊。","s":"The next day, we got up early and went to the beach again to swim and play in the sand."},{"w":"What are you going to do next weekend?","p":"conj.","d":"next · 其他用法","c":"你下個週末要做什麼？","s":"Are you going to visit your grandmother next weekend, or will you stay home and study for the test?"},{"w":"We went shopping. After that, we had lunch at a noodle shop.","p":"conj.","d":"after that · 順序","c":"我們去購物。之後，在麵店吃午餐。","s":"We played basketball in the park for an hour, and after that, we ate ice cream at a small shop."},{"w":"He finished his homework. After that, he played video games.","p":"conj.","d":"after that · 順序","c":"他寫完作業。之後，他打電動。","s":"Kevin finished his math homework at seven, and after that, he helped his mother wash the dishes."},{"w":"We visited the museum. After that, we went to the night market.","p":"conj.","d":"after that · 順序","c":"我們參觀博物館。之後，我們去夜市。","s":"We walked around the old temple in the morning, and after that, we had lunch at a famous noodle shop."},{"w":"I'm busy now. I will call you back later.","p":"conj.","d":"later · 順序","c":"我現在很忙。我晚點再回電給你。","s":"I can't talk now because I am in class, but I will call you back later this afternoon."},{"w":"They got married in 2010. Two years later, they had a baby.","p":"conj.","d":"later · 順序","c":"他們 2010 年結婚。兩年後，他們有了孩子。","s":"My parents moved to this city in 2005, and three years later, I was born in the hospital nearby."},{"w":"See you later! Don't forget our meeting.","p":"conj.","d":"later · 其他用法","c":"待會見！別忘了我們的會面。","s":"See you later at the basketball game, and don't forget to bring your water bottle and a towel."},{"w":"Sooner or later, you will have to tell him the truth.","p":"conj.","d":"later · 其他用法","c":"你遲早得告訴他實話。","s":"Sooner or later, your parents will find out about the broken window, so you should tell them now."},{"w":"I'll explain it to you later on.","p":"conj.","d":"later · 其他用法","c":"我晚點再跟你解釋。","s":"I don't understand this math question now, but the teacher will explain it to us later on."},{"w":"Please hand in your paper no later than Friday.","p":"conj.","d":"later · 其他用法","c":"請最晚在星期五前交報告。","s":"Please hand in your reports no later than Friday, or the teacher will take ten points off."},{"w":"see you later (待會見) / sooner or later (遲早) / later on (之後) / no later than (不晚於)","p":"conj.","d":"later · 其他用法","c":"later 的片語整理","s":"See you later on at the party, and sooner or later we will find a gift for Amy."},{"w":"He came back two hours later. / He came back after two hours. / He will come back in two hours.","p":"conj.","d":"later · 易混淆","c":"他兩小時後回來了。／他兩小時後回來了。／他兩小時後會回來。","s":"Grandpa went out for a walk at six, and two hours later he came home with fresh bread."}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"finally – if","cards":[{"w":"We waited for an hour. Finally, the bus came.","p":"conj.","d":"finally · 順序","c":"我們等了一小時。終於，公車來了。","s":"We waited outside the movie theater in the rain for an hour, and finally the doors opened."},{"w":"Finally, don't forget to turn off the lights before you leave.","p":"conj.","d":"finally · 順序","c":"最後，離開前別忘了關燈。","s":"Finally, remember to bring your lunch box and water tomorrow, because the school trip will be long."},{"w":"finally","p":"conj.","d":"finally · 順序","c":"最後（順序）或終於（等待很久）=finally 有「最後」和「終於」兩義","s":"After looking for my cat all night, I finally found her sleeping in a box in the garden."},{"w":"We waited and finally the show began. / Finally, remember to lock the door.","p":"conj.","d":"finally · 易混淆","c":"我們等著，表演終於開始了。／最後，記得鎖門。","s":"The students waited in a long line, and finally the school gates opened for the sports day."},{"w":"After a long trip, we got home at last.","p":"conj.","d":"at last · 順序","c":"經過漫長的旅程，我們終於到家了。","s":"After three long hours on the train, we got to Grandma's house in the mountains at last."},{"w":"At last, the rain stopped and the sun came out.","p":"conj.","d":"at last · 順序","c":"終於，雨停了，太陽出來了。","s":"At last, the long winter was over, and the flowers in the park started to open again."},{"w":"at last","p":"conj.","d":"at last · 順序","c":"終於（經過等待），不是「最後一點」=at last 強調等待很久","s":"We waited for the bus in the rain for almost an hour, and at last it came around the corner."},{"w":"At last the bus came. / At the end of the class, the bell rang. / In the end, we won. / Lastly, thank you all.","p":"conj.","d":"at last · 易混淆","c":"公車終於來了。／下課時鐘響了。／最後我們贏了。／最後，謝謝大家。","s":"At last Dad came home, and at the end of dinner he told us that in the end he got the job."},{"w":"We talked for hours. In the end, we decided to stay home.","p":"conj.","d":"in the end · 順序","c":"我們談了好幾個小時。最後，我們決定待在家。","s":"We looked at many shoes in the department store for two hours, but in the end my sister bought nothing."},{"w":"In the end, the team won the game by one point.","p":"conj.","d":"in the end · 順序","c":"最後，這隊以一分贏了比賽。","s":"The two teams played very hard in the rain, and in the end our school won the game by two points."},{"w":"In the end, everything turned out fine for us.","p":"conj.","d":"in the end · 總結","c":"最後，我們的一切都很順利。","s":"The typhoon was strong and we were worried about our old house, but in the end nothing was broken."},{"w":"In the end, she chose to study in Taipei.","p":"conj.","d":"in the end · 總結","c":"最後，她選擇在臺北讀書。","s":"My brother thought about many different jobs for a long time, and in the end he decided to become a cook."},{"w":"In the end, we won. / At the end of the street, there is a park. / By the end of this month, I will finish the book.","p":"conj.","d":"in the end · 易混淆","c":"最後我們贏了。／街的盡頭有個公園。／這個月底前我會讀完這本書。","s":"In the end, my family moved to a small town, and at the end of our street there is a quiet park."},{"w":"At first, I didn't like the city. Now I love it.","p":"conj.","d":"at first · 順序","c":"起初，我不喜歡這城市。現在我愛上它了。","s":"At first the new student was very shy and quiet, but now she talks and laughs with everyone in class."},{"w":"At first, the work was hard, but it got easier.","p":"conj.","d":"at first · 順序","c":"起初，工作很難，但後來變簡單了。","s":"At first I could not swim at all, but after one summer of lessons I can swim across the pool."},{"w":"at first","p":"conj.","d":"at first · 順序","c":"起初（暗示後來改變）=at first 暗示後來情況改變","s":"At first my little brother hated the taste of green vegetables, but now he eats them at every meal."},{"w":"Last but not least, I want to thank my parents.","p":"conj.","d":"last but not least · 順序","c":"最後但同樣重要的是，我要感謝我的父母。","s":"I want to thank my teachers, my friends, and last but not least, my mother, who always believes in me."},{"w":"Last but not least, remember to bring your ID card.","p":"conj.","d":"last but not least · 順序","c":"最後但同樣重要的是，記得帶身分證。","s":"For the trip, bring water, a hat, some snacks, and last but not least, your student card for the train ticket."},{"w":"She was laughing and crying at the same time.","p":"conj.","d":"at the same time · 時間","c":"她同時又笑又哭。","s":"My mother can talk on the phone and cook dinner for the whole family at the same time without any trouble."},{"w":"Two babies were born at the same time last night.","p":"conj.","d":"at the same time · 時間","c":"昨晚有兩個寶寶同時出生。","s":"The two boys crossed the line at the same time, so the judges had to watch the video again."},{"w":"I want to help him, but at the same time I am very busy.","p":"conj.","d":"at the same time · 對比","c":"我想幫他，但同時我也很忙。","s":"I really want to join the basketball team, but at the same time I need more hours to study for the exam."},{"w":"The job is hard. At the same time, it pays well.","p":"conj.","d":"at the same time · 對比","c":"這工作很辛苦。但同時，薪水不錯。","s":"Living in a big city is exciting and convenient, but at the same time it is noisy and costs a lot."},{"w":"at the same time (同時，時間) 也可表「但同時、然而」(對比)","p":"conj.","d":"at the same time · 對比","c":"at the same time 可表轉折","s":"My new phone takes great pictures, but at the same time it is so heavy that my pocket feels full."},{"w":"If it rains tomorrow, we will stay at home.","p":"conj.","d":"if · 條件","c":"如果明天下雨，我們就待在家。","s":"If the weather is nice this Saturday, my family will ride bicycles along the river and have a picnic."},{"w":"If you heat ice, it turns into water.","p":"conj.","d":"if · 條件","c":"如果你加熱冰，它會變成水。","s":"If you leave ice cream outside on a hot summer day, it turns into a sweet little pool in a few minutes."},{"w":"If I were you, I would tell the teacher the truth.","p":"conj.","d":"if · 條件","c":"如果我是你，我會告訴老師實話。","s":"If I were you, I would say sorry to Mary right now before she goes home and feels sad all night."},{"w":"if 子句用現在式表未來；If I were you 表與事實相反","p":"conj.","d":"if · 條件","c":"if 子句不用 will","s":"If it snows in the mountains next week, we will take warm coats, and if I were rich, I would fly there."},{"w":"I don't know if she will come to the party.","p":"conj.","d":"if · 其他用法","c":"我不知道她會不會來派對。","s":"Linda is not sure if her cousin will join the school trip to Tainan, because he has a cold this week."},{"w":"Call me if necessary. I'm home all day.","p":"conj.","d":"if · 其他用法","c":"如果需要就打給我。我整天在家。","s":"Keep this medicine in your bag and take one pill if necessary, but do not take more than two a day."},{"w":"Are you free tonight? If so, let's see a movie.","p":"conj.","d":"if · 其他用法","c":"你今晚有空嗎？如果有，我們去看電影。","s":"Do you have time after school today? If so, let's go to the night market and try the new noodle stand."},{"w":"If not, we can meet tomorrow instead.","p":"conj.","d":"if · 其他用法","c":"如果沒有，我們可以改明天見。","s":"I hope the library is open on Sunday morning; if not, we can study at my house instead and order pizza."},{"w":"What if it rains on the picnic day?","p":"conj.","d":"if · 其他用法","c":"如果野餐那天下雨怎麼辦？","s":"We planned a big birthday party for Grandma in the park, but what if it rains hard all day on Saturday?"},{"w":"if","p":"conj.","d":"if · 其他用法","c":"whether (是否，間接問句)；if so (如果是) / if not (如果不是) / if necessary (如有需要) / what if (如果…怎麼辦) / even if / only if / as if=if 的片語整理","s":"Ask her if she needs help; if so, stay late, and if not, go home, but if necessary, call me."},{"w":"if (是否) 不可與 or not 直接連用；whether or not 可以","p":"conj.","d":"if · 易混淆","c":"if 與 whether 的差別","s":"The teacher asked if we understood the lesson, and then she asked us whether or not we needed more time."},{"w":"I wonder whether or not he will come. (不說 if or not)","p":"conj.","d":"if · 易混淆","c":"我想知道他會不會來。","s":"I wonder whether or not the new bakery sells birthday cakes, and if it does, let's buy one for Dad."},{"w":"if 子句表未來用現在式；If I were you… 表與事實相反","p":"conj.","d":"if · 易混淆","c":"if 條件句的時態","s":"If my dad gets home early tonight, we will eat out, and if I were older, I would drive us there myself."}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"unless – when","cards":[{"w":"You will be late unless you leave right now.","p":"conj.","d":"unless · 條件","c":"除非你現在就走，否則你會遲到。","s":"Unless you finish your vegetables, Mom will not let you have the chocolate cake she made this afternoon."},{"w":"Unless it rains, we will have the picnic on Sunday.","p":"conj.","d":"unless · 條件","c":"除非下雨，我們星期天要去野餐。","s":"Unless the typhoon changes direction tonight, all schools in Taipei will be closed tomorrow morning."},{"w":"I won't go unless you come with me.","p":"conj.","d":"unless · 條件","c":"除非你跟我一起去，否則我不去。","s":"My little sister will not go into the dark room unless someone turns on the light and holds her hand."},{"w":"unless","p":"conj.","d":"unless · 條件","c":"if…not（除非）=unless 等於 if not","s":"You cannot get into the pool unless you wear a cap on your head, so please buy one at the front desk."},{"w":"You can stay here as long as you keep quiet.","p":"conj.","d":"as long as · 條件","c":"只要你保持安靜，你可以待在這裡。","s":"You can borrow my new comic books as long as you give them back to me clean before next Monday."},{"w":"As long as you try your best, I will be happy.","p":"conj.","d":"as long as · 條件","c":"只要你盡力，我就會開心。","s":"As long as everyone in the class brings a snack to share, our Friday party will be fun and cheap."},{"w":"as long as (只要) 也可表「和…一樣長」","p":"conj.","d":"as long as · 條件","c":"as long as 有條件和長度兩義","s":"Dad says we can keep the puppy as long as we walk it, and its tail is as long as my hand."},{"w":"The river is as long as three hundred kilometers.","p":"conj.","d":"as long as · 其他用法","c":"這條河長達三百公里。","s":"The new bridge across the river is as long as ten school buses, so it takes a while to walk over it."},{"w":"My hair is not as long as yours.","p":"conj.","d":"as long as · 其他用法","c":"我的頭髮沒有你的長。","s":"My school day is not as long as my brother's, because his high school lessons end at five every day."},{"w":"Take an umbrella in case it rains later.","p":"conj.","d":"in case · 條件","c":"帶把傘，以防晚點下雨。","s":"Please pack a jacket in your bag in case the weather turns cold on the mountain this weekend."},{"w":"Write down my number in case you need help.","p":"conj.","d":"in case · 條件","c":"記下我的電話，以防你需要幫忙。","s":"I will give you my sister's phone number in case you cannot find our house in the dark tonight."},{"w":"In case of fire, use the stairs and leave the building quickly.","p":"conj.","d":"in case · 條件","c":"如果發生火災，走樓梯並快速離開大樓。","s":"In case of an earthquake, get under a strong desk, cover your head, and stay away from the windows."},{"w":"in case + 句子；in case of + N","p":"conj.","d":"in case · 條件","c":"in case of 後接名詞","s":"Take some extra money in case the tickets cost more, and in case of rain, the game moves inside."},{"w":"Study hard. Otherwise, you will fail the test.","p":"conj.","d":"otherwise · 條件","c":"努力讀書。否則，你會考不及格。","s":"Please water the plants every morning while I am away; otherwise, they will die in this hot weather."},{"w":"Wear a coat. Otherwise, you will catch a cold.","p":"conj.","d":"otherwise · 條件","c":"穿上外套。否則，你會感冒。","s":"You should bring an umbrella to school today; otherwise, you will get wet on your way home this afternoon."},{"w":"otherwise (句首加逗號)","p":"conj.","d":"otherwise · 條件","c":"or（否則）=otherwise 等於命令句後的 or","s":"Hurry up and get on the train now; otherwise, we will miss the first hour of the big show in Taichung."},{"w":"The soup was a little cold but otherwise very good.","p":"conj.","d":"otherwise · 其他用法","c":"湯有點冷，但除此之外非常好。","s":"The hotel room was a little small, but otherwise it was clean and comfortable, with a view of the sea."},{"w":"He thinks the plan is good, but I think otherwise.","p":"conj.","d":"otherwise · 其他用法","c":"他認為這計畫很好，但我不這麼認為。","s":"Most students in my class think the new teacher is too serious, but my good friend Amy and I think otherwise."},{"w":"otherwise","p":"conj.","d":"otherwise · 其他用法","c":"在其他方面／不同地 (think otherwise = 想法不同)=otherwise 的其他意思","s":"Everyone says the movie is boring, but I think otherwise, and otherwise the night was fun for all of us."},{"w":"You can go out only if you finish your homework.","p":"conj.","d":"only if · 條件","c":"只有在你完成作業的情況下才能出去。","s":"You may play computer games tonight only if you finish all your homework and practice the piano first."},{"w":"Only if you practice every day will you get better.","p":"conj.","d":"only if · 條件","c":"只有每天練習，你才會進步。","s":"Only if we leave the house before six in the morning will we catch the first train to the beach."},{"w":"Only if… 放句首時，主句要倒裝","p":"conj.","d":"only if · 條件","c":"only if 句首時主句倒裝","s":"Only if you eat breakfast every day will you have enough energy for your morning lessons at school."},{"w":"When I got home, my mother was cooking dinner.","p":"conj.","d":"when · 時間","c":"我回到家時，媽媽正在煮晚餐。","s":"When the teacher walked into the room, all the students were talking loudly about the baseball game."},{"w":"Call me when you get to the station.","p":"conj.","d":"when · 時間","c":"你到車站時打給我。","s":"Please send me a short message when you arrive at the airport so that I can drive over to pick you up."},{"w":"When I was a kid, I wanted to be a doctor.","p":"conj.","d":"when · 時間","c":"我小時候想當醫生。","s":"When my grandfather was a young boy, he walked two hours to school every day because there were no buses."},{"w":"when 子句用現在式表未來","p":"conj.","d":"when · 時間","c":"when 子句不用 will","s":"When the show ends tonight, we will take a taxi home, because the last bus leaves at ten thirty."},{"w":"When is your birthday? — It's on May second.","p":"conj.","d":"when · 其他用法","c":"你的生日是什麼時候？——五月二日。","s":"When does the winter vacation begin this year, and when will you come back from your trip to Japan?"},{"w":"I don't know when the movie will start.","p":"conj.","d":"when · 其他用法","c":"我不知道電影什麼時候開始。","s":"Nobody in our class knows when the new English teacher will arrive, so we are all excited and curious."},{"w":"Since when do you like coffee?","p":"conj.","d":"when · 其他用法","c":"你從什麼時候開始喜歡咖啡了？","s":"Since when do you get up at five in the morning to jog, because you always loved sleeping late?"},{"w":"I was about to leave when the phone rang.","p":"conj.","d":"when · 其他用法","c":"我正要離開時電話響了。","s":"We were about to cut the birthday cake when the lights went out and the whole room became dark."},{"w":"when 當疑問詞 (什麼時候) / 間接問句 (when + 未來式可用 will) / be about to…when (正要…就)","p":"conj.","d":"when · 其他用法","c":"when 疑問詞與連接詞的差別","s":"When is the party, and when will she arrive, because we were about to leave when she finally called us?"},{"w":"when 子句表「未來」不用 will，但間接問句的 when 可用 will","p":"conj.","d":"when · 易混淆","c":"when 兩種用法的時態","s":"Please call me when you get home, because I really do not know when the heavy rain will stop tonight."},{"w":"Call me when you arrive. / I don't know when he will arrive.","p":"conj.","d":"when · 易混淆","c":"你到了打給我。／我不知道他什麼時候會到。","s":"Tell Mom when you finish your test, but I do not know when the teacher will give us our scores."}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"whenever – until","cards":[{"w":"Whenever I feel sad, I listen to music.","p":"conj.","d":"whenever · 時間","c":"每當我難過時，我就聽音樂。","s":"Whenever my grandmother visits us from Tainan, she brings a big box of cookies she makes herself for the whole family."},{"w":"You can call me whenever you need help.","p":"conj.","d":"whenever · 時間","c":"你需要幫忙時隨時可以打給我。","s":"You are welcome to visit our new house whenever you like, because the door is always open for old friends."},{"w":"whenever","p":"conj.","d":"whenever · 時間","c":"every time（每當）／at any time（隨時）=whenever 有「每當」和「隨時」兩義","s":"Whenever it rains, my dog hides under the bed, so you can come and play with him whenever the sun is out."},{"w":"Brush your teeth before you go to bed.","p":"conj.","d":"before · 時間","c":"睡覺前要刷牙。","s":"Please wash your hands with soap before you touch the food, because your fingers are dirty after playing outside."},{"w":"Before I left, I turned off all the lights.","p":"conj.","d":"before · 時間","c":"離開前，我關掉了所有的燈。","s":"Before the typhoon arrived, my father closed all the windows and put the bicycles inside the house."},{"w":"It will be a long time before we meet again.","p":"conj.","d":"before · 時間","c":"要很久我們才會再見面。","s":"It will be a long time before my little cousin can ride a bicycle without help from his parents."},{"w":"It + be + 時間 + before…（要…才…）","p":"conj.","d":"before · 時間","c":"before 可表「要過多久才」","s":"It was three years before my uncle visited us again, because he was working in a hospital in America."},{"w":"I have seen this movie before.","p":"conj.","d":"before · 其他用法","c":"我以前看過這部電影。","s":"I am sure I have met that tall man before, but I cannot remember his name or where we met."},{"w":"It won't be long before the summer vacation starts.","p":"conj.","d":"before · 其他用法","c":"不久暑假就要開始了。","s":"It will not be long before the weather gets warm and the flowers in the park begin to open again."},{"w":"The day before yesterday was my birthday.","p":"conj.","d":"before · 其他用法","c":"前天是我的生日。","s":"The day before yesterday, my sister and I baked a chocolate cake for Mom, and it tasted really good."},{"w":"Please stand before the mirror and look at yourself.","p":"conj.","d":"before · 其他用法","c":"請站在鏡子前面看看自己。","s":"The little girl stood before the big mirror in the store and smiled at her new pink dress for a long time."},{"w":"before 當副詞 (以前) / 介係詞 (在…之前：before dinner, before long) / 連接詞 (在…之前)","p":"conj.","d":"before · 其他用法","c":"before 的三種詞性","s":"I have been to Taipei before, and before dinner tonight we will go there again before the stores close."},{"w":"After the rain stopped, we went out to play.","p":"conj.","d":"after · 時間","c":"雨停後，我們出去玩。","s":"After the movie ended, we walked to a noodle shop near the theater and talked about the story for an hour."},{"w":"I will call you after I finish my homework.","p":"conj.","d":"after · 時間","c":"我寫完作業後會打給你。","s":"My father will take us to the night market after he gets home from work and takes a quick shower."},{"w":"What do you usually do after school?","p":"conj.","d":"after · 其他用法","c":"你放學後通常做什麼？","s":"After school, my friends and I usually play basketball in the park until our mothers call us home."},{"w":"The students left the classroom one after another.","p":"conj.","d":"after · 其他用法","c":"學生們一個接一個離開教室。","s":"The children ran into the pool one after another, and soon the water was full of happy shouts and laughs."},{"w":"I have to look after my little sister this weekend.","p":"conj.","d":"after · 其他用法","c":"這週末我得照顧我妹妹。","s":"My mother asked me to look after my baby brother while she went to the supermarket to buy some milk."},{"w":"We will leave the day after tomorrow.","p":"conj.","d":"after · 其他用法","c":"我們後天出發。","s":"We will fly to Japan the day after tomorrow, so I still have two days to pack my bags for the trip."},{"w":"The boy was named after his grandfather.","p":"conj.","d":"after · 其他用法","c":"這男孩是以他祖父的名字命名的。","s":"My little cousin was named after her grandmother, so both of them share the same beautiful name, Mary."},{"w":"after 當介係詞：after school / one after another (一個接一個) / look after (照顧) / the day after tomorrow (後天) / name A after B (以 B 為 A 命名) / after all (畢竟)","p":"conj.","d":"after · 其他用法","c":"after 的介係詞片語","s":"After school, we looked after the puppy one after another, and after all, it will be big the day after tomorrow."},{"w":"I will call you as soon as I get home.","p":"conj.","d":"as soon as · 時間","c":"我一到家就會打給你。","s":"As soon as the rain stops, we will run to the park and play basketball before it gets too dark."},{"w":"As soon as the bell rang, the students ran out.","p":"conj.","d":"as soon as · 時間","c":"鐘聲一響，學生們就跑出去。","s":"As soon as the teacher left the room, the students began to talk and laugh about the funny video."},{"w":"As soon as he saw the dog, he started to cry.","p":"conj.","d":"as soon as · 時間","c":"他一看到那隻狗就開始哭。","s":"As soon as my mother smelled the smoke from the kitchen, she ran to turn off the stove and open the window."},{"w":"as soon as 子句用現在式表未來（一…就…）","p":"conj.","d":"as soon as · 時間","c":"as soon as 子句不用 will","s":"Mom will start cooking dinner as soon as she gets home, so please set the table before she arrives."},{"w":"I will wait here until you come back.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 時間","c":"我會在這裡等到你回來。","s":"My grandmother always waits at the door until everyone in the family comes home safely from school and work."},{"w":"She didn't go to bed until midnight last night.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 時間","c":"她昨晚直到半夜才睡。","s":"The children did not stop playing video games until their father came home and turned off the TV."},{"w":"Let's wait here until the rain stops.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 時間","c":"我們在這裡等到雨停吧。","s":"Let's stay inside the bookstore until the heavy rain stops, and then we can walk home and stay dry."},{"w":"not…until","p":"conj.","d":"until · 時間","c":"直到…才；until 子句用現在式表未來=not until 表「直到才」","s":"My little brother did not learn to swim until he was ten, but now he swims faster than anyone in our family."},{"w":"The store is open until nine every night.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 其他用法","c":"這家店每晚營業到九點。","s":"The new coffee shop near our school is open until eleven at night, so students often study there after dinner."},{"w":"Up until now, I have never been late for school.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 其他用法","c":"直到現在，我上學從沒遲到過。","s":"Up until now, my grandmother has never used a cellphone, but she wants to learn so she can see our photos."},{"w":"Wait until then, and I will tell you the secret.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 其他用法","c":"等到那時候，我會告訴你那個秘密。","s":"The movie starts at seven, so wait until then, and I will buy the popcorn and drinks for everyone."},{"w":"until 當介係詞 + 時間 (直到…)；up until now (直到現在) / until then (直到那時)","p":"conj.","d":"until · 其他用法","c":"until 介係詞用法","s":"Up until now I have been busy, but the shop is open until ten, so wait until then and we will go."},{"w":"I will stay here until ten. / I will finish the work by ten.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 易混淆","c":"我會待到十點。／我會在十點前完成工作。","s":"I will wait for you at the bus stop until six, but please try to finish your piano lesson by five thirty."},{"w":"not…until (直到…才)","p":"conj.","d":"until · 易混淆","c":"Not until…+ 倒裝=not until 句型","s":"Not until the teacher turned on the lights did the students see the big birthday cake on her desk."},{"w":"He didn't leave until his mom came.","p":"conj.","d":"until · 易混淆","c":"Not until his mom came did he leave.=直到他媽媽來他才離開。","s":"Not until my mother called my name three times did I finally put down the comic book and come to dinner."}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"till – all in all","cards":[{"w":"We played basketball in the park till it got dark.","p":"conj.","d":"till · 時間","c":"我們在公園打籃球打到天黑。","s":"My cousins and I watched the stars on the roof till our parents told us it was time to go to sleep."},{"w":"Keep going straight till you see the post office.","p":"conj.","d":"till · 時間","c":"一直直走，直到你看到郵局。","s":"Walk along this street till you see a big red temple, and the night market is just behind it."},{"w":"till","p":"conj.","d":"till · 時間","c":"until（口語較常用）=till 等於 until","s":"We talked and laughed on the phone till midnight, so this morning both of us were very sleepy in class."},{"w":"Once you learn to ride a bike, you never forget.","p":"conj.","d":"once · 時間","c":"一旦你學會騎腳踏車，就永遠不會忘。","s":"Once you taste my grandmother's beef noodles, you will never want to eat at any other restaurant again."},{"w":"Once the rain stops, we can go out and play.","p":"conj.","d":"once · 時間","c":"一旦雨停，我們就可以出去玩。","s":"Once the test is over this Friday, my friends and I are going to sing at a KTV all afternoon."},{"w":"I go swimming once a week with my friends.","p":"conj.","d":"once · 其他用法","c":"我每週和朋友去游泳一次。","s":"My family eats dinner at a nice restaurant once a month to celebrate everyone's hard work and good grades."},{"w":"Once upon a time, there was a king who had three sons.","p":"conj.","d":"once · 其他用法","c":"很久很久以前，有一個國王有三個兒子。","s":"Once upon a time, a poor young farmer lived with his mother in a small house at the foot of a mountain."},{"w":"I once lived in Tainan for two years.","p":"conj.","d":"once · 其他用法","c":"我曾經在臺南住過兩年。","s":"My English teacher once worked in a hotel in America, so she tells us many interesting stories about her job."},{"w":"We eat out once in a while, not every day.","p":"conj.","d":"once · 其他用法","c":"我們偶爾出去吃，不是每天。","s":"We do not often watch movies at the theater, but once in a while my dad buys tickets for the whole family."},{"w":"Come here at once! The dinner is ready.","p":"conj.","d":"once · 其他用法","c":"馬上過來！晚餐好了。","s":"The kitchen is on fire, so call the fire department at once and get everyone out of the house quickly!"},{"w":"once 當副詞：once a week (一次) / once (曾經) / once upon a time (從前) / once in a while (偶爾) / at once (馬上) / all at once (突然)","p":"conj.","d":"once · 其他用法","c":"once 副詞與片語整理","s":"I once came to this park once a week, and all at once I remember the trees, so let's sit down."},{"w":"By the time we got there, the movie had started.","p":"conj.","d":"by the time · 時間","c":"我們到那裡時，電影已經開始了。","s":"By the time the fire truck arrived at the old building, the family had already run out through the back door."},{"w":"By the time you wake up, I will be at work.","p":"conj.","d":"by the time · 時間","c":"你醒來時，我已經在上班了。","s":"By the time you finish reading this long letter, I will be on the plane and on my way to Japan."},{"w":"by the time + 過去式，主句常用過去完成式","p":"conj.","d":"by the time · 時間","c":"by the time 常搭配完成式","s":"By the time we arrived at the train station, the last train to Tainan had already left ten minutes earlier."},{"w":"Every time I see him, he is reading a book.","p":"conj.","d":"every time · 時間","c":"每次我看到他，他都在看書。","s":"Every time my father cooks dinner, the kitchen becomes very dirty, but the food always tastes wonderful."},{"w":"She gets nervous every time she takes a test.","p":"conj.","d":"every time · 時間","c":"她每次考試都會緊張。","s":"My little sister cries every time she hears thunder, so Mom holds her close during every summer storm."},{"w":"The moment she saw the gift, she smiled.","p":"conj.","d":"the moment · 時間","c":"她一看到禮物就笑了。","s":"The moment the bell rang for lunch, all the hungry students rushed out of the room toward the cafeteria."},{"w":"I knew him the moment I heard his voice.","p":"conj.","d":"the moment · 時間","c":"我一聽到他的聲音就認出他了。","s":"My dog starts to jump and bark with joy the moment he hears my father's car in front of our house."},{"w":"the moment","p":"conj.","d":"the moment · 時間","c":"as soon as（一…就…）=the moment 等於 as soon as","s":"The moment the teacher said the test was over, Tom put down his pencil and smiled as soon as he could."},{"w":"I'm busy at the moment. Can you call back in a moment?","p":"conj.","d":"the moment · 易混淆","c":"我現在很忙。你可以等一下再打來嗎？","s":"My mother is cooking at the moment, so please call back in a moment, and she will talk to you then."},{"w":"The moment I saw her, I knew she was the one.","p":"conj.","d":"the moment · 易混淆","c":"我一看到她，就知道她是我要找的人。","s":"The moment I walked into the new school, I knew that I would make a lot of good friends there."},{"w":"After a while, the baby stopped crying and fell asleep.","p":"conj.","d":"after a while · 時間","c":"過了一會兒，寶寶停止哭泣睡著了。","s":"The sky was dark and the wind was strong, but after a while the clouds moved away and the sun came out."},{"w":"We waited, and after a while the doctor came out.","p":"conj.","d":"after a while · 時間","c":"我們等著，過了一會兒醫生出來了。","s":"At first the puppy was afraid of us, but after a while it walked over slowly and licked my hand."},{"w":"The food was bad and the service was slow. In short, don't go there.","p":"conj.","d":"in short · 總結","c":"食物難吃，服務又慢。總之，別去那裡。","s":"The hotel was dirty, the food was cold, and the beach was far away; in short, our trip was a big mistake."},{"w":"In short, we need more time and more money.","p":"conj.","d":"in short · 總結","c":"總之，我們需要更多時間和更多錢。","s":"In short, if you want to do well on the test, you should sleep early, eat breakfast, and review your notes."},{"w":"In a word, the trip to Japan was wonderful.","p":"conj.","d":"in a word · 總結","c":"一句話，這次日本之旅太棒了。","s":"The weather was perfect, the food was delicious, and the people were friendly; in a word, the trip was great."},{"w":"In a word, he is the best teacher I have ever had.","p":"conj.","d":"in a word · 總結","c":"一句話，他是我遇過最好的老師。","s":"In a word, my grandmother is the kindest person I know, because she always helps her neighbors with a smile."},{"w":"All in all, it was a great day at the beach.","p":"conj.","d":"all in all · 總結","c":"總的來說，這是在海邊美好的一天。","s":"It rained a little in the morning, but all in all, our school trip to the zoo was a wonderful day."},{"w":"All in all, the new restaurant is worth a try.","p":"conj.","d":"all in all · 總結","c":"總的來說，這家新餐廳值得一試。","s":"The new department store is a little far from home, but all in all, it is a good place for a Sunday."}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"in fact – even","cards":[{"w":"He looks young. In fact, he is already fifty years old.","p":"conj.","d":"in fact · 強調","c":"他看起來很年輕。事實上，他已經五十歲了。","s":"Many people think my grandfather is quiet and serious, but in fact he tells the funniest jokes at every family dinner."},{"w":"I don't hate dogs. In fact, I have two at home.","p":"conj.","d":"in fact · 強調","c":"我不討厭狗。事實上，我家有兩隻。","s":"My sister says she does not like sweets, but in fact she eats a piece of chocolate cake almost every night."},{"w":"The test wasn't hard. In fact, it was quite easy.","p":"conj.","d":"in fact · 強調","c":"考試不難。事實上，相當簡單。","s":"The hike up the mountain looked hard from below, but in fact it took us only forty minutes to reach the top."},{"w":"in fact 常用來補充或修正前句","p":"conj.","d":"in fact · 強調","c":"in fact 用來說明「其實」","s":"Everyone thinks Mark is bad at sports, but in fact he won first place in the school swim race last year."},{"w":"I thought he was from Japan. Actually, he is from Korea.","p":"conj.","d":"actually · 語氣轉換","c":"我以為他來自日本。其實，他來自韓國。","s":"Many people think my mother is from Japan because of her name, but actually she was born and raised in Tainan."},{"w":"Actually, I don't like coffee very much. I prefer tea.","p":"conj.","d":"actually · 語氣轉換","c":"其實，我不太喜歡咖啡。我比較喜歡茶。","s":"I know you want to take the bus, but actually the subway is faster and cheaper during the busy morning hours."},{"w":"Actually, the meeting is on Tuesday, not Monday.","p":"conj.","d":"actually · 語氣轉換","c":"其實，會議是星期二，不是星期一。","s":"Actually, the museum is closed on Mondays, so we should change our plan and visit it on Tuesday instead."},{"w":"actually 常用來禮貌地糾正或說出實情","p":"conj.","d":"actually · 語氣轉換","c":"actually 用來委婉糾正","s":"Actually, I did not break the window, because I was at the library with Amy when it happened this afternoon."},{"w":"Can I borrow your pen? Of course, here you are.","p":"conj.","d":"of course · 強調","c":"我可以借你的筆嗎？當然，給你。","s":"Can I use your computer to finish my report tonight? Of course, but please turn it off when you are done."},{"w":"Of course, you can stay here as long as you want.","p":"conj.","d":"of course · 強調","c":"當然，你想待多久就待多久。","s":"Of course you can bring your little brother to the party, because there will be games and cake for the kids too."},{"w":"Of course not. I would never lie to you.","p":"conj.","d":"of course · 強調","c":"當然不會。我絕不會對你說謊。","s":"Did you eat the last piece of pizza without asking? Of course not, I was at school all afternoon with Lisa."},{"w":"He stayed up all night. No wonder he is so sleepy.","p":"conj.","d":"no wonder · 強調","c":"他熬夜整晚。難怪他這麼睏。","s":"Jack played basketball in the hot sun for three hours, so no wonder he drank three bottles of water at dinner."},{"w":"It's raining. No wonder there are so few people here.","p":"conj.","d":"no wonder · 強調","c":"在下雨。難怪這裡人這麼少。","s":"The bakery gives away free cookies every Friday afternoon, so no wonder there is always a long line outside."},{"w":"No wonder she is angry. You forgot her birthday!","p":"conj.","d":"no wonder · 強調","c":"難怪她生氣。你忘了她的生日！","s":"No wonder you feel so cold; you came to school in a thin shirt even though it is only ten degrees outside."},{"w":"no wonder + 句子","p":"conj.","d":"no wonder · 強調","c":"難怪…（前句說原因）=no wonder 前句為原因","s":"My brother studied English for two hours every night this month, so no wonder he got a perfect score on the test."},{"w":"Eat well, sleep well, and above all, stay happy.","p":"conj.","d":"above all · 強調","c":"吃得好，睡得好，最重要的是，保持開心。","s":"On the trip, take photos, try the local food, make new friends, and above all, stay safe and call home every night."},{"w":"Above all, remember to be kind to others.","p":"conj.","d":"above all · 強調","c":"最重要的是，記得對別人友善。","s":"A good student listens in class, finishes homework on time, and above all, never gives up when things get hard."},{"w":"above all","p":"conj.","d":"above all · 強調","c":"最重要的是（放在一連串事項的最後）=above all 用在列舉的最後","s":"For the picnic we need fruit, drinks, a big blanket, and above all, good weather, so let's hope the sun comes out."},{"w":"I love all kinds of fruit, especially mangoes in summer.","p":"conj.","d":"especially · 強調","c":"我愛各種水果，尤其是夏天的芒果。","s":"My grandmother loves all kinds of flowers, especially the yellow ones that grow in her garden every spring."},{"w":"The roads are busy, especially during rush hour.","p":"conj.","d":"especially · 強調","c":"路上很忙，尤其是在尖峰時間。","s":"The night market is always crowded, especially on Saturday nights when many families come out to eat together."},{"w":"It was so cold that even the river froze.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 強調","c":"冷到連河都結冰了。","s":"The math test was so hard that even the smartest student in our class could not finish all the questions."},{"w":"The little boy can't even write his own name.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 強調","c":"那個小男孩連自己的名字都不會寫。","s":"My little brother is so lazy on weekends that he does not even get out of bed to eat his breakfast."},{"w":"Even a small child can understand this simple story.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 強調","c":"即使是小孩也能懂這個簡單的故事。","s":"Even my grandmother, who is eighty years old, can send messages and take pictures with her new cellphone."},{"w":"even (甚至，副詞) ≠ even though／even if（連接詞）","p":"conj.","d":"even · 強調","c":"even 本身是副詞","s":"It was raining so hard that even the brave dog hid under the table, though it usually loves to play outside."},{"w":"Two, four, and six are even numbers.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 其他用法","c":"二、四、六是偶數。","s":"The teacher asked us to write down all the even numbers from two to twenty on the board before the bell."},{"w":"The road is even, so it is easy to ride a bike here.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 其他用法","c":"路面很平，所以在這裡騎腳踏車很容易。","s":"The path around the lake is even and wide, so even small children can ride their bicycles there safely."},{"w":"It was raining. Even so, we still went hiking.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 其他用法","c":"在下雨。即使如此，我們還是去爬山了。","s":"The restaurant was expensive and far from the station; even so, we had a wonderful dinner there last night."},{"w":"Even now, I still remember my first teacher.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 其他用法","c":"即使到現在，我仍然記得我的第一位老師。","s":"Even now, many years after I left that small town, I still remember the taste of the fresh bread from the bakery."},{"w":"even 當形容詞","p":"conj.","d":"even · 其他用法","c":"偶數的／平的；even so (即使如此) / even now (即使現在) / not even (連…都不)=even 形容詞與片語","s":"The road is even, the numbers are even, and even now he cannot even ride a bike; even so, he keeps trying."},{"w":"Even a kid knows it. / Even though he is a kid, he knows it. / Even if he were a kid, he would know it.","p":"conj.","d":"even · 易混淆","c":"連小孩都知道。／儘管他是小孩，他也知道。／即使他是小孩，他也會知道。","s":"Even a small bird knows the way home, and even though the sky was dark, ours flew back even if tired."}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"by the way – honestly","cards":[{"w":"By the way, have you seen my blue jacket?","p":"conj.","d":"by the way · 語氣轉換","c":"對了，你有看到我的藍色夾克嗎？","s":"I will bring the snacks for the movie night, and by the way, did you remember to invite Tom and his sister?"},{"w":"By the way, what time does the movie start tonight?","p":"conj.","d":"by the way · 語氣轉換","c":"對了，今晚電影幾點開始？","s":"By the way, the English teacher said the test is next Wednesday, not Friday, so we should start studying tonight."},{"w":"By the way, happy birthday! I almost forgot.","p":"conj.","d":"by the way · 語氣轉換","c":"對了，生日快樂！我差點忘了。","s":"Thanks for helping me carry the boxes, and by the way, your mother called and wants you home before six."},{"w":"by the way 用來轉換話題或補充（順便一提）","p":"conj.","d":"by the way · 語氣轉換","c":"by the way 用來換話題","s":"We will meet at the park at ten tomorrow; by the way, do you know a good place for lunch near there?"},{"w":"I lost my wallet. Luckily, a kind man found it.","p":"conj.","d":"luckily · 語氣轉換","c":"我丟了錢包。幸運的是，一位好心人找到了。","s":"I fell off my bicycle on the way to school today, but luckily I was not hurt and my bag was fine."},{"w":"Luckily, no one was hurt in the car accident.","p":"conj.","d":"luckily · 語氣轉換","c":"幸運的是，車禍中沒人受傷。","s":"Our bus broke down on the highway for an hour; luckily, a kind driver stopped and gave everyone cold water."},{"w":"Luckily, the rain stopped before the game began.","p":"conj.","d":"luckily · 語氣轉換","c":"幸運的是，比賽開始前雨停了。","s":"The little boy forgot his lunch at home, but luckily his friend Peter shared a sandwich and an apple with him."},{"w":"Fortunately, I caught the last train home last night.","p":"conj.","d":"fortunately · 語氣轉換","c":"幸好，我昨晚趕上了回家的最後一班火車。","s":"Fortunately, my mother found my lost wallet under the car seat before we left for the airport this morning."},{"w":"Fortunately, the doctor said it was nothing serious.","p":"conj.","d":"fortunately · 語氣轉換","c":"幸好，醫生說沒什麼嚴重的。","s":"The baby fell down the stairs, but fortunately she only cried for a minute and had no cuts on her body."},{"w":"Unfortunately, the store was closed when we got there.","p":"conj.","d":"unfortunately · 語氣轉換","c":"不幸的是，我們到的時候商店關門了。","s":"Unfortunately, the heavy rain did not stop all day, so we had to cancel our class trip to the beach."},{"w":"Unfortunately, I failed my driving test again last week.","p":"conj.","d":"unfortunately · 語氣轉換","c":"不幸的是，我上週又沒通過駕照考試。","s":"My sister practiced hard for the school music show for two months, but unfortunately she got sick on the big day."},{"w":"I'd love to come, but unfortunately I have to work.","p":"conj.","d":"unfortunately · 語氣轉換","c":"我很想來，但很遺憾我得工作。","s":"I would love to join your birthday dinner on Saturday, but unfortunately my family will be in Japan that week."},{"w":"Sadly, our old dog died last winter at the age of fifteen.","p":"conj.","d":"sadly · 語氣轉換","c":"遺憾的是，我們的老狗去年冬天以十五歲高齡過世了。","s":"Sadly, the old tree in front of our school fell down during the typhoon, and the birds lost their home."},{"w":"Sadly, the team lost the final game by one point.","p":"conj.","d":"sadly · 語氣轉換","c":"遺憾的是，這隊以一分之差輸了決賽。","s":"Sadly, my best friend moved to Kaohsiung last month, so now we can only talk on the phone every night."},{"w":"The old man smiled sadly and walked away.","p":"conj.","d":"sadly · 其他用法","c":"老人悲傷地笑了笑，然後走開了。","s":"The little girl waved sadly at the train window as her grandmother went back to her home in the small town."},{"w":"She looked at the broken toy sadly.","p":"conj.","d":"sadly · 其他用法","c":"她難過地看著壞掉的玩具。","s":"The old man looked sadly at the empty house where he had lived with his wife for more than fifty years."},{"w":"Surprisingly, the little boy won the race easily.","p":"conj.","d":"surprisingly · 語氣轉換","c":"令人驚訝的是，那個小男孩輕鬆贏了比賽。","s":"Surprisingly, the quiet girl who never talks in class sang the loudest and best at the school music show."},{"w":"Surprisingly, the cheap restaurant had the best food.","p":"conj.","d":"surprisingly · 語氣轉換","c":"令人驚訝的是，那家便宜的餐廳食物最好吃。","s":"Surprisingly, the small shop at the corner sells the most delicious dumplings in the whole city of Taipei."},{"w":"Hopefully, it will be sunny on our picnic day.","p":"conj.","d":"hopefully · 語氣轉換","c":"希望野餐那天會是晴天。","s":"Hopefully, the rain will stop before the baseball game tomorrow, so our team can finally play the final match."},{"w":"Hopefully, the doctor can see you this afternoon.","p":"conj.","d":"hopefully · 語氣轉換","c":"希望醫生今天下午能幫你看診。","s":"Hopefully, the rain will stop before noon, so we can still have our picnic in the park with the whole class."},{"w":"Clearly, he didn't read the test question carefully.","p":"conj.","d":"clearly · 語氣轉換","c":"顯然，他沒有仔細讀考題。","s":"Clearly, Tom did not study for the math test last night, because he could not answer even the first question."},{"w":"Clearly, she is the best singer in the class.","p":"conj.","d":"clearly · 語氣轉換","c":"顯然，她是班上最棒的歌手。","s":"Clearly, Mary is the fastest runner on our team, so the coach always lets her run the last part of the race."},{"w":"Please speak clearly so that everyone can hear you.","p":"conj.","d":"clearly · 其他用法","c":"請說清楚，這樣大家才能聽到你。","s":"The teacher asked us to speak slowly and clearly when we read the story aloud in front of the class."},{"w":"I can see the mountains clearly from my window.","p":"conj.","d":"clearly · 其他用法","c":"我從窗戶可以清楚地看到山。","s":"After the heavy rain stopped, we could see the tall buildings and green hills clearly from the top of the mountain."},{"w":"Honestly, I don't think this plan will work.","p":"conj.","d":"honestly · 語氣轉換","c":"老實說，我不認為這計畫行得通。","s":"Honestly, I do not think we can finish this big project by Friday if we only meet once a week."},{"w":"Honestly, the movie was not as good as people say.","p":"conj.","d":"honestly · 語氣轉換","c":"老實說，這部電影沒有大家說的那麼好。","s":"Honestly, the new restaurant near our school is too expensive, and the noodles there do not taste very special."},{"w":"Please answer the question honestly.","p":"conj.","d":"honestly · 其他用法","c":"請誠實地回答這個問題。","s":"My mother always tells me to answer her questions honestly, even when I know she will not be happy."},{"w":"He has always lived honestly and worked hard.","p":"conj.","d":"honestly · 其他用法","c":"他一直誠實生活、努力工作。","s":"My grandfather lived honestly all his life, and he never took anything that did not belong to him."}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"to tell the truth – on the whole","cards":[{"w":"To tell the truth, I didn't finish the book.","p":"conj.","d":"to tell the truth · 語氣轉換","c":"老實說，我沒讀完這本書。","s":"To tell the truth, I did not understand the movie at all, but I did not want to say so in front of my friends."},{"w":"To tell the truth, I don't really like your new hat.","p":"conj.","d":"to tell the truth · 語氣轉換","c":"老實說，我不太喜歡你的新帽子。","s":"To tell the truth, the cake you made tastes a little too sweet for me, but the cookies are really delicious."},{"w":"To be honest, I forgot about our meeting.","p":"conj.","d":"to be honest · 語氣轉換","c":"老實說，我忘了我們的會面。","s":"To be honest, I did not enjoy the long bus ride to the beach, because I felt sick the whole way."},{"w":"To be honest, I think the blue one looks better.","p":"conj.","d":"to be honest · 語氣轉換","c":"老實說，我覺得藍色的比較好看。","s":"To be honest, I think the red dress looks much better on you than the green one you tried on first."},{"w":"In my opinion, students should have less homework.","p":"conj.","d":"in my opinion · 語氣轉換","c":"在我看來，學生的作業應該少一點。","s":"In my opinion, every student should learn to cook at least one simple dish before they finish high school."},{"w":"In my opinion, this is the best pizza in town.","p":"conj.","d":"in my opinion · 語氣轉換","c":"在我看來，這是鎮上最好吃的披薩。","s":"In my opinion, riding a bike to school is better than taking the bus, because it is cheaper and healthier."},{"w":"He always talks as if he knew everything.","p":"conj.","d":"as if · 語氣轉換","c":"他說話總是好像他什麼都知道。","s":"My little brother talks about the game as if he were the best player in the whole world, but he just started."},{"w":"She looked as if she were going to cry.","p":"conj.","d":"as if · 語氣轉換","c":"她看起來好像要哭了。","s":"When the teacher called her name, Mary looked as if she had not heard a single word of the lesson."},{"w":"It looks as if it is going to rain.","p":"conj.","d":"as if · 語氣轉換","c":"看起來好像要下雨了。","s":"The sky is getting dark and the wind is blowing hard, so it looks as if a storm is coming tonight."},{"w":"as if + 過去式（與事實相反）；as if + 現在式（可能為真）","p":"conj.","d":"as if · 語氣轉換","c":"as if 後接過去式表與事實相反","s":"He spends money as if he were rich, but it looks as if he is going to lose his job soon."},{"w":"Well, I'm not sure. Let me think about it.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 語氣轉換","c":"嗯，我不確定。讓我想一想。","s":"Well, I am not sure if the store is still open, so let me call them before we leave the house."},{"w":"Well, that's all for today. See you tomorrow.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 語氣轉換","c":"好，今天就到這裡。明天見。","s":"Well, that is the end of our class today, so please remember to bring your workbooks tomorrow morning."},{"w":"well (句首語氣詞) ≠ well (副詞：好地)","p":"conj.","d":"well · 語氣轉換","c":"well 在句首表停頓或轉換","s":"Well, I did not do very well on the test, but my teacher said I am getting better every week."},{"w":"She speaks English very well for a ten-year-old.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 其他用法","c":"以十歲的孩子來說，她英文說得很好。","s":"Although my grandmother never went to school, she can read and write Chinese very well and loves poems."},{"w":"I don't feel well today. I think I have a cold.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 其他用法","c":"我今天覺得不舒服。我想我感冒了。","s":"Jenny did not feel well after lunch, so the nurse told her to lie down and rest for an hour."},{"w":"Get well soon! We miss you at school.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 其他用法","c":"早日康復！我們在學校很想你。","s":"We all hope you get well soon, because the basketball team needs you for the big game next week."},{"w":"Well done! You answered every question right.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 其他用法","c":"做得好！你每題都答對了。","s":"Well done, everyone! You worked so hard this month that our class won first place in the school art show."},{"w":"The farmers get water from a deep well.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 其他用法","c":"農夫們從一口深井取水。","s":"In the old days, people in this small village had to walk a long way to get water from a well."},{"w":"well 當副詞 (好地) / 形容詞 (健康的：feel well, get well) / 名詞 (井)；well done (做得好) / as well (也) / may as well (不妨)","p":"conj.","d":"well · 其他用法","c":"well 的多種詞性","s":"My sister sings very well, and she plays the piano as well, so we may as well ask her to sing for us."},{"w":"She is a good singer, and she sings well.","p":"conj.","d":"well · 易混淆","c":"她是個好歌手，而且她唱得好。","s":"Mary is a good dancer, and she dances so well that everyone stopped talking to watch her on the stage."},{"w":"The hotel was small, but at least it was clean.","p":"conj.","d":"at least · 語氣轉換","c":"飯店很小，但至少很乾淨。","s":"The weather was cold and wet during our trip, but at least we did not get lost in the mountains."},{"w":"At least you tried. Don't feel bad about it.","p":"conj.","d":"at least · 語氣轉換","c":"至少你試過了。別難過。","s":"You did not win the race today, but at least you finished it, and that is something to be proud of."},{"w":"There were at least fifty people at the party.","p":"conj.","d":"at least · 其他用法","c":"派對上至少有五十個人。","s":"We need at least twenty chairs for the party tonight, because more people are coming than we first thought."},{"w":"You should drink at least eight glasses of water a day.","p":"conj.","d":"at least · 其他用法","c":"你一天至少應該喝八杯水。","s":"The doctor told my father to walk at least thirty minutes every day if he wants to stay healthy."},{"w":"In general, people in Taiwan are very friendly.","p":"conj.","d":"in general · 總結","c":"一般來說，臺灣的人非常友善。","s":"In general, students in our school like sports such as basketball and badminton more than quiet games like chess."},{"w":"In general, kids like sweet food more than adults do.","p":"conj.","d":"in general · 總結","c":"一般來說，小孩比大人更喜歡甜食。","s":"In general, the weather in Taipei is wet and cool in winter, so people often carry an umbrella with them."},{"w":"On the whole, the students did well on the test.","p":"conj.","d":"on the whole · 總結","c":"整體來說，學生們考得不錯。","s":"On the whole, the school trip to the museum was a success, although the bus arrived twenty minutes late."},{"w":"On the whole, I enjoyed the trip very much.","p":"conj.","d":"on the whole · 總結","c":"整體來說，我非常享受這次旅行。","s":"On the whole, the new students in my class are kind and friendly, and only one or two of them are a little shy."}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"and so on – in turn","cards":[{"w":"She likes many sports, like hiking, swimming, and so on.","p":"conj.","d":"and so on · 舉例","c":"她喜歡很多運動，像爬山、游泳等等。","s":"At the night market you can buy many kinds of snacks, such as fried chicken, fruit, ice cream, and so on."},{"w":"He sleeps late, that is to say, he goes to bed after midnight.","p":"conj.","d":"that is to say · 舉例","c":"他睡得晚，也就是說，他半夜過後才上床。","s":"My uncle works at night, that is to say, he starts his job at ten in the evening and comes home at six."},{"w":"The shop is open every day, that is to say, seven days a week.","p":"conj.","d":"that is to say · 舉例","c":"這家店每天營業，也就是說，一週七天。","s":"This ticket is good for the whole weekend, that is to say, you can visit the park both on Saturday and Sunday."},{"w":"I would stay home rather than go out in the rain.","p":"conj.","d":"rather than · 對比","c":"我寧願待在家，而不要在雨中出門。","s":""},{"w":"She chose tea rather than coffee this morning.","p":"conj.","d":"rather than · 對比","c":"今天早上她選了茶而非咖啡。","s":"For breakfast this morning, Tom chose a bowl of rice and eggs rather than the bread and milk he usually eats."},{"w":"The teacher asked each student a question in turn.","p":"conj.","d":"in turn · 順序","c":"老師輪流問每個學生一個問題。","s":"At the school show, the students in each class walked up to the stage in turn and sang a short song."},{"w":"Please answer the questions in turn, one by one.","p":"conj.","d":"in turn · 順序","c":"請一個一個輪流回答問題。","s":"During the game, the children sat in a circle and rolled the big ball to each other in turn."},{"w":"Prices went up. This, in turn, made people buy less.","p":"conj.","d":"in turn · 因果","c":"物價上漲。這反過來使人們買得更少。","s":"The factory closed last year, and this, in turn, made many families in the town move to the city for work."},{"w":"He helped me, and I, in turn, helped my little brother.","p":"conj.","d":"in turn · 因果","c":"他幫了我，而我也接著幫了我弟弟。","s":"My teacher taught me how to swim, and I, in turn, taught my little cousin at the pool last summer."},{"w":"She was kind to them, and they in turn were kind to her.","p":"conj.","d":"in turn · 因果","c":"她對他們好，他們也反過來對她好。","s":"The old man was friendly to the children, and they in turn brought him fruit and cookies every weekend."},{"w":"in turn (反過來、接著、進而) 表前因導致後果或接續動作","p":"conj.","d":"in turn · 因果","c":"in turn 可表「反過來、接著」","s":"Tom slept late last night, and this in turn made him miss the school bus and arrive late for class."},{"w":"The students read the poem in turn.","p":"conj.","d":"in turn · 易混淆","c":"學生們輪流朗讀這首詩。","s":"In music class, each of us sang one line of the song in turn until we finished the whole song together."}]}];
